1
00:02:09,181 --> 00:02:14,002
No living creature was harmed during
the production of this tv show.

2
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,159
Osman.

3
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,639
I will never kneel before you.

4
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,199
Here is the battlefield.

5
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,039
I will cut your face under the mask...

6
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:28,759
...in half!

7
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,279
Bala.

8
00:02:40,960 --> 00:02:42,519
I'm with you, my Osman!

9
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,759
I'm here too, father.

10
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:51,359
Alps! For Baysungur! For our martyrs!

11
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:53,279
For our vengeance!

12
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:56,479
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

13
00:02:56,640 --> 00:03:01,479
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

14
00:03:01,560 --> 00:03:03,759
-O Allah!
-Attack!

15
00:03:03,760 --> 00:03:05,159
-O Allah!
-Attack!

16
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,999
Come.

17
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:47,479
I will make you pay for
attempting to kill my daughter!

18
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:50,999
I'll kill you in front of your daughter's eyes.

19
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:10,839
Brother, your double swords
can't compete with my solo.

20
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,599
You admire my swords! Come on!

21
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,639
Come on!

22
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,919
Brother!

23
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:36,359
Brother? Cerkutay? Brother?

24
00:04:36,600 --> 00:04:38,119
My brother...

25
00:04:38,280 --> 00:04:40,679
What did you do, brother?

26
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:44,239
Well, brother... I became
worthy of my double swords.

27
00:04:44,240 --> 00:04:46,399
Oh brother... Oh Cerkutay...

28
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:49,279
-Boran.
-Yes, brother?

29
00:04:49,320 --> 00:04:51,759
Come closer.

30
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,719
You should know this.

31
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:59,759
Cerkutay never dies.

32
00:05:00,240 --> 00:05:04,159
You know, my heart is on the
right. This can't kill me.

33
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:07,479
You madman!

34
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,199
Let's go.

35
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:12,439
-Let's stick our swords into their hearts.
-Here we go.

36
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:14,479
Watch out!

37
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:20,599
-Get me up.
-Come, brother.

38
00:05:22,080 --> 00:05:25,519
Cerkutay. This will hurt. Come on.

39
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,319
It hurt!

40
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:31,959
You're good.

41
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:35,439
You envied my double swords
and now I'm left with only one!

42
00:05:48,040 --> 00:05:50,359
Allah is the greatest!

43
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:33,839
-Thank you, son.
-Thank you, my Bey. Come on, alps!

44
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,839
Come on, brothers!

45
00:07:05,530 --> 00:07:10,039
You masked devil! Show yourself.
Who are you?

46
00:07:22,560 --> 00:07:24,159
Fatma.

47
00:07:38,160 --> 00:07:40,959
Fatma... Get up, dear.

48
00:07:41,160 --> 00:07:45,039
-Are you alright? All good?
-I'm fine, mother.

49
00:07:45,040 --> 00:07:46,799
Stay back.

50
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,239
Come on, come on.

51
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,159
Here we go.

52
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:15,519
You'll pay for setting me
up with your life, Bayhan.

53
00:08:18,600 --> 00:08:20,359
Father!

54
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,959
-Die!
-Saruca!

55
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:35,479
Saruca! My son!

56
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:38,158
-Saruca?
-My son.

57
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:41,119
-My son. -Lukas.

58
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,039
Lukas!

59
00:08:48,280 --> 00:08:50,119
My son.

60
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:25,799
Alps!

61
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:28,719
This smoke is toxic! Draw back!

62
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:35,679
Alaaddin! Take care of Saruca!

63
00:09:35,880 --> 00:09:40,879
-As you order, my Bey!
-Alps, this way!

64
00:10:02,320 --> 00:10:04,239
My Bey, I'm curious.

65
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:07,119
You haven't told me why we're going to Sogut.

66
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:13,159
A storm broke out in Sogut. Osman got disgraced.

67
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:16,559
And you're still asking me why we're going?

68
00:10:17,800 --> 00:10:19,599
Don't you get it, Sancar?

69
00:10:19,760 --> 00:10:22,879
They broke Osman's unbreakable pride.

70
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:26,239
We're going there to see his disgrace.

71
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:29,119
Okay, my Bey.

72
00:10:30,600 --> 00:10:33,599
Here is my order, Sancar.

73
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:37,279
In the honor of Osman's losing Sogut,

74
00:10:37,280 --> 00:10:42,439
...we'll hold a great feast and
offer food to beys and people.

75
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:45,679
As you order, my Bey.

76
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,999
How could that happen?

77
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:57,039
How did they save Fatma from Akhisar?

78
00:10:57,200 --> 00:11:00,199
I swear I'll kill everyone who made mistakes.

79
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:02,199
This way.

80
00:11:04,840 --> 00:11:06,519
Sofia

81
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,439
Run! Run!

82
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:20,879
Yusuf, go ahead of them from the right side.

83
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:22,839
-As you order, my Bey.
-Alps!

84
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:28,799
-Bala, you all go that way.
-Be careful, my Bey.

85
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:31,119
Let's go!

86
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:44,759
Let them come. We will see.

87
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,679
Run! Run!

88
00:11:55,040 --> 00:11:57,799
You vile dog!

89
00:11:58,920 --> 00:12:02,359
You asked for this.

90
00:12:09,840 --> 00:12:13,439
Osman Bey has sent us here but...

91
00:12:13,680 --> 00:12:16,279
...the heathens aren't around here.

92
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:28,279
Alps, we're going to the left side.

93
00:12:41,240 --> 00:12:43,039
Your death is here.

94
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,639
You can't run anywhere!

95
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,439
Attack!

96
00:14:04,960 --> 00:14:08,359
We should go, commander.
Our soldiers can stop Osman.

97
00:14:08,800 --> 00:14:10,919
My Bey, they are running off!

98
00:14:16,640 --> 00:14:19,519
Yusuf is there! They can't go anywhere!

99
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:21,999
I will kill them!

100
00:14:28,640 --> 00:14:31,279
Boran, Cerkutay. Follow him!

101
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:40,319
Neither Lukas nor that snake
can survive in the woods!

102
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:45,919
Run, commander. Save yourself.

103
00:15:05,080 --> 00:15:06,719
Sofia.

104
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,479
Sofia, stop.

105
00:15:16,880 --> 00:15:19,279
That's Karesi Bey. Karesi Bey!

106
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:42,879
Karesi Bey.

107
00:15:46,200 --> 00:15:49,239
You said you would take Sogut from Osman.

108
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:51,239
Lukas?

109
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:52,879
What happened?

110
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:56,199
No time for this. Osman is after
us. We need to get out of here.

111
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:58,479
Give us your horses.

112
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:02,079
We have to go, Lukas.
Osman can be here any minute.

113
00:16:02,440 --> 00:16:06,639
Is this the woman you mentioned?

114
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:09,039
Yes, it's me.

115
00:16:09,320 --> 00:16:11,079
Why hide your face?

116
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:13,519
Help us.

117
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:17,719
Or get out of our way, Karesi Bey.

118
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,519
You can go.

119
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:26,319
But you can't survive in the woods without me.

120
00:16:26,840 --> 00:16:29,959
And you can't beat Osman without us, Karesi Bey.

121
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,839
You either help us now...

122
00:16:31,960 --> 00:16:34,119
...or lose your best ally.

123
00:16:46,800 --> 00:16:50,999
-Get in the carriage.
-Sofia, come on. Come on.

124
00:17:04,040 --> 00:17:06,559
You can never..

125
00:17:07,680 --> 00:17:10,479
Saruca! Saruca! My son!

126
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,679
Open your eyes! Come on!

127
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:16,079
Open your eyes! -Alps! Hold the streets!

128
00:17:16,560 --> 00:17:19,117
Ensure Sogut's safety, come on! Come on!

129
00:17:20,839 --> 00:17:21,877
Saruca

130
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,439
Open your eyes!

131
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:27,759
Open your eyes, my son

132
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:33,119
Bayhan Bey! Bayhan Bey! What are you doing?

133
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:36,119
If you take that dagger out, we
cannot stop the bleeding. Don't!

134
00:17:36,120 --> 00:17:38,679
What are we going to do?
-Let go! Don't touch it!

135
00:17:38,680 --> 00:17:40,359
What are we going to do?

136
00:17:40,360 --> 00:17:42,119
Press it on the wound.

137
00:17:42,120 --> 00:17:43,919
Alright, I am doing it!

138
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,839
Saruca, breathe, Saruca!

139
00:17:47,440 --> 00:17:51,479
Saruca, breathe!
-Alaeddin, how is he?

140
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:54,519
The poisonous smoke hurt his lungs, brother.

141
00:17:54,520 --> 00:17:56,399
I cannot do anything here!

142
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:58,359
The medicines are in the tribe.

143
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,559
We need to go to the tribe! Come on!

144
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,959
Will you save my son, Alaeddin?

145
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:06,119
-Will you save him?
-He will be alright, God willing.. Alps!

146
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:07,919
Bring the cart here!

147
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:10,399
We will take Saruca to the tribe, come on!

148
00:18:10,400 --> 00:18:14,359
Come on! Let's go!
-I will come with you.

149
00:18:16,400 --> 00:18:19,319
We cannot know what these dastard dogs will do.

150
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:21,279
Come on! Hurry!
-Hang on, my son!

151
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:25,159
Hang on Saruca! Hang on my son!

152
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:27,919
Lower the stretcher quickly!

153
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:33,159
Hang on. -Help! Come on!

154
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,839
Come on! Bring it here!

155
00:18:36,880 --> 00:18:42,039
Come on! Come on! Hang on!

156
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,079
Here!

157
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,199
Push

158
00:18:48,880 --> 00:18:50,919
Come on! Come on Alps!

159
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:54,119
Come on Bayhan Bey! Hurry!

160
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:58,639
Hurry!

161
00:18:58,640 --> 00:19:00,079
Come on!

162
00:19:09,240 --> 00:19:11,159
I hear voices there... Come on.

163
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:17,719
My Bey...

164
00:19:24,080 --> 00:19:26,079
What are you doing here?

165
00:19:26,080 --> 00:19:27,679
We were waiting, my Bey.

166
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:31,319
We decided to hold the left
side since Lukas didn't come.

167
00:19:31,320 --> 00:19:32,079
How?

168
00:19:37,720 --> 00:19:38,759
I gave you a duty.

169
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:41,999
Did you do what you decided on your own?

170
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:43,679
My Bey...

171
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:53,239
The infidels ran away from where you were.

172
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:57,199
You cannot disobey the state.

173
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:05,039
Don't you do it again.

174
00:20:13,240 --> 00:20:15,279
Is there a trace?

175
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:19,919
There is no trace of Lukas, my Bey.

176
00:20:19,920 --> 00:20:23,239
We've also lost the trail
of that jackal named Hristo.

177
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:26,599
But we heard something
from a shepherd on the way.

178
00:20:26,640 --> 00:20:30,039
A horse-drawn cart was heading north, they said.

179
00:20:30,880 --> 00:20:32,719
What if it's Lukas, Osman?

180
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:34,399
We will find out, my Bala.

181
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:39,119
-We will find out. Aykurt!
-My Bey! -Bring the horses!

182
00:20:39,120 --> 00:20:40,079
Yes my Bey.

183
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:44,119
We'll take a better road than
the forest. We'll go there faster.

184
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,239
Okay my Bey.

185
00:20:55,880 --> 00:21:00,639
Hang on... Hang on... Come on! Saruca!

186
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:02,399
Hang on my son!

187
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,119
Saruca. My son..

188
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,759
Hang on..

189
00:21:06,760 --> 00:21:09,199
Hang on my son... We are almost there!

190
00:21:09,720 --> 00:21:12,319
My Allah, keep my son with me!

191
00:21:12,320 --> 00:21:14,119
Saruca is strong Bayhan Bey

192
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:16,359
You'll see. He will recover.

193
00:21:17,440 --> 00:21:20,559
Alaeddin, Alaeddin Bey, will my son live?

194
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:23,319
Pull yourself together, Bayhan Bey!

195
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:25,639
We will be strong first. Calm down!

196
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:32,359
Father...

197
00:21:32,920 --> 00:21:34,599
Saruca!

198
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:36,919
Saruca!

199
00:21:37,840 --> 00:21:39,519
Saruca!

200
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,639
Saruca! My son..

201
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:46,199
Hold it here. Press with your hand.

202
00:21:46,200 --> 00:21:48,679
Do it firmly, Bayhan Bey...
-Father...

203
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:51,359
Saruca... -Come on Alaeddin

204
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:55,839
Hang on Saruca, we will
arrive in the tribe soon!

205
00:21:56,080 --> 00:21:56,879
Father..

206
00:21:56,880 --> 00:22:02,119
Saruca... Why did you do
this? Why did you do this, son?

207
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:04,799
Why did you risk your life for me?

208
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,359
Don't you say that...

209
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:09,879
...I am incompetent?

210
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,799
-What is the value of my life?
-Don't talk like that.

211
00:22:17,320 --> 00:22:19,079
You are a piece of my heart!

212
00:22:24,160 --> 00:22:27,119
I waited for so long to
hear this from you, father.

213
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:33,439
Even if I die, I won't feel sorry now.

214
00:22:33,950 --> 00:22:35,799
Saruca.

215
00:22:36,560 --> 00:22:37,639
Saruca.

216
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:39,319
Saruca!

217
00:22:39,600 --> 00:22:44,379
Open your eyes! Saruca! My son!

218
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:47,159
Come on! Hang on my son!

219
00:22:47,160 --> 00:22:49,159
Come on Alaeddin Bey! Hurry!

220
00:23:11,600 --> 00:23:12,719
My Bey, Osman Bey!

221
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,479
Karesi Bey...

222
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:29,839
What are you doing in Sogut?

223
00:23:30,400 --> 00:23:32,039
What are you doing here?

224
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,559
I heard that..

225
00:23:36,160 --> 00:23:38,399
...you were in a difficult position.

226
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:41,119
You were going to give...

227
00:23:42,240 --> 00:23:45,519
...Sogut to the infidels
for your daughter's life.

228
00:23:46,320 --> 00:23:48,839
Even if you see me as your enemy...

229
00:23:49,040 --> 00:23:51,759
...I came here to help you but...

230
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:54,319
...you handled it yourself.

231
00:23:55,960 --> 00:23:57,479
What is it?

232
00:23:58,080 --> 00:24:00,199
Are you going to protect us now?

233
00:24:00,760 --> 00:24:01,999
Yes, yes.

234
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:04,879
When it's about children..

235
00:24:05,440 --> 00:24:07,719
...I don't look for enmity.

236
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:12,319
I came here to find the
middle way between you...

237
00:24:12,880 --> 00:24:17,439
...and the infidels who you say I work
with and to save your daughter's life.

238
00:24:18,520 --> 00:24:20,679
But I see that..

239
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,559
..there is no need for that.

240
00:24:24,280 --> 00:24:27,439
May you recover soon, my daughter Fatma Hatun.

241
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:35,119
Thank you Karesi Bey.
Thank you, thank you.

242
00:24:35,120 --> 00:24:36,999
But we cannot know for sure.

243
00:24:37,400 --> 00:24:42,559
Maybe you are trying to find the middle
way for those who you want to protect, huh?

244
00:24:43,120 --> 00:24:44,599
Don't worry.

245
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:48,079
Today, you will hear
their screams in the forest.

246
00:24:50,680 --> 00:24:55,359
I won't ask anyone to
spare the life of an infidel.

247
00:24:55,920 --> 00:25:01,119
Just because we traded with
them, you think we are the same.

248
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:05,359
You are responsible for this, Osman.

249
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:11,359
You think of frontiers as a hunting ground...

250
00:25:11,840 --> 00:25:14,439
...and us as the prey you chase.

251
00:25:15,560 --> 00:25:17,959
But if we were united..

252
00:25:19,120 --> 00:25:21,599
...if we did politics together...

253
00:25:22,240 --> 00:25:25,039
...if we ruled the frontiers together...

254
00:25:25,280 --> 00:25:28,199
...if we hunted the infidels together...

255
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:32,839
...would we need any
allies other than ourselves?

256
00:25:34,400 --> 00:25:37,159
So you are talking about hunting them huh?

257
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:40,599
We are also hunting, Karesi Bey.

258
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:43,079
We are after a couple of jackals.

259
00:25:50,480 --> 00:25:51,719
Open that door!

260
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:56,159
What is it?

261
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:58,399
Karesi Bey.

262
00:26:12,610 --> 00:26:14,519
Osman Bey.

263
00:26:14,520 --> 00:26:16,479
Stop there.

264
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:20,719
I came here for your daughter's life.

265
00:26:21,240 --> 00:26:26,039
-Are you accusing me of hiding an infidel?
-Karesi Bey.

266
00:26:27,760 --> 00:26:30,279
If there's nothing you are afraid of...

267
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:33,799
...why are you standing against me, huh?

268
00:26:35,440 --> 00:26:36,799
Move.

269
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,679
Move Karesi Bey.

270
00:26:59,760 --> 00:27:01,879
Open the door.

271
00:27:05,240 --> 00:27:07,039
Open the door!

272
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:34,959
My Bey, Osman Bey is coming this way!

273
00:27:36,520 --> 00:27:39,239
Lukas, get out, now!

274
00:27:39,600 --> 00:27:42,359
We'll meet after Osman is gone. Come on!

275
00:27:52,360 --> 00:27:55,039
Our intentions are good, but...

276
00:27:55,440 --> 00:27:57,959
What will happen to your disrespect...

277
00:27:58,240 --> 00:28:02,079
...and ungratefulness Osman?

278
00:28:02,920 --> 00:28:06,639
You want to stay enemies. What a pity.

279
00:28:10,880 --> 00:28:15,919
As long as you step on my land without my
permission, this is how you will be treated.

280
00:28:18,320 --> 00:28:19,999
Leave now.

281
00:28:28,840 --> 00:28:30,159
Okay Osman Bey.

282
00:28:33,920 --> 00:28:35,589
Okay.

283
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:43,479
Saruca, my son! Hang on! My son!

284
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:48,399
They are coming... They
won't be able to survive here.

285
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:50,599
Go ahead and inform the doctors.

286
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:53,119
Have them prepare everything.
-Yes my Bey.

287
00:28:56,280 --> 00:28:57,959
Hang on, my son!

288
00:28:59,960 --> 00:29:01,559
Ambush!

289
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:03,239
I will take my son's revenge!

290
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,639
You stay there!

291
00:29:05,120 --> 00:29:07,519
I will deal with those dogs alone.

292
00:29:20,920 --> 00:29:22,879
Stay with your son, Bayhan Bey!

293
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:25,239
Oh Allah! -Go!

294
00:29:31,640 --> 00:29:34,639
Convey my greetings to those in hell.

295
00:29:34,640 --> 00:29:37,839
Tell them you failed as well!

296
00:29:39,520 --> 00:29:41,159
Father...

297
00:29:51,400 --> 00:29:52,799
He cannot breathe!

298
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:55,319
Saruca is not alright, brother! We need to go!

299
00:29:55,320 --> 00:29:57,959
You go! Go!

300
00:29:57,960 --> 00:30:02,439
Come on Bayhan Bey! Come on!

301
00:30:02,440 --> 00:30:05,479
Come on! We don't have time! He is bleeding!

302
00:30:05,480 --> 00:30:07,679
Come on Alps! Come on!

303
00:30:16,160 --> 00:30:18,159
Come at me!

304
00:30:42,640 --> 00:30:43,879
Alps!

305
00:30:44,320 --> 00:30:46,439
Go ahead and secure the area!

306
00:30:55,120 --> 00:30:56,539
He is coming.

307
00:31:27,760 --> 00:31:31,799
You got out of the carriage
just in time. If you hadn't...

308
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:35,119
...we would have fought with Osman.

309
00:31:35,320 --> 00:31:38,679
You will get something in
return for this favor, Karesi Bey.

310
00:31:38,680 --> 00:31:40,519
Of course I will.

311
00:31:41,960 --> 00:31:47,719
You would never help us if you wouldn't
get anything from this anyway, Karesi Bey.

312
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:54,519
Don't boast for no reason.

313
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:02,879
You're a smart Hatun(Woman).

314
00:32:04,080 --> 00:32:06,719
We will do so many things with you.

315
00:32:08,800 --> 00:32:13,119
But I want to see the faces
of those I will work with.

316
00:32:14,680 --> 00:32:17,759
Now tell me. Who are you?

317
00:32:23,290 --> 00:32:24,919
Take it off..

318
00:32:25,600 --> 00:32:27,839
Let me see your face.

319
00:32:48,200 --> 00:32:50,679
My name is Sofia.

320
00:32:52,840 --> 00:32:55,919
You will have to pay the
price of seeing my face.

321
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:01,239
Karesi Bey.

322
00:33:22,040 --> 00:33:26,319
They know we'll take Sogut and
that they won’t get out of this forest.

323
00:33:26,560 --> 00:33:29,239
They must have found a hole to hide, my Bey.

324
00:33:35,560 --> 00:33:37,239
They left our lands.

325
00:33:40,120 --> 00:33:40,959
How?

326
00:33:40,959 --> 00:33:44,239
They left our lands with the help of Karesi Bey!

327
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:03,039
Here..

328
00:34:03,560 --> 00:34:07,239
The tracks come this way.
The intensity of the tracks...

329
00:34:07,240 --> 00:34:08,918
...increases in this area.

330
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:11,638
Clearly...

331
00:34:11,760 --> 00:34:13,438
..he let someone in here.

332
00:34:14,520 --> 00:34:17,918
We saw it with our own eyes,
Osman Bey. The carriage was empty.

333
00:34:18,000 --> 00:34:20,399
They must have sensed we were coming...

334
00:34:20,520 --> 00:34:22,559
...and got out of the carriage.

335
00:34:23,040 --> 00:34:24,918
Then he let them in again.

336
00:34:26,560 --> 00:34:28,478
With Karesi Bey's protection...

337
00:34:28,600 --> 00:34:30,319
...they left our lands.

338
00:34:32,199 --> 00:34:33,518
Don't...

339
00:34:33,960 --> 00:34:35,399
...don't you have any shame?

340
00:34:35,960 --> 00:34:37,679
Don't you have any shame?

341
00:34:37,679 --> 00:34:39,719
How could you protect the infidel?

342
00:34:40,840 --> 00:34:42,239
Let it be so.

343
00:34:42,639 --> 00:34:44,319
Let it be so Karesi Bey.

344
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:46,079
-Boran.
-My Bey.

345
00:34:46,080 --> 00:34:47,638
Send envoys to the Beys.

346
00:34:47,840 --> 00:34:50,399
We will gather the council. Now..

347
00:34:51,040 --> 00:34:53,039
..it is time to end this.

348
00:34:53,600 --> 00:34:55,319
Yes my Bey.

349
00:34:56,320 --> 00:34:57,599
Karesi Bey.

350
00:35:36,960 --> 00:35:37,719
Well..

351
00:35:39,560 --> 00:35:42,799
Now you are free.

352
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:46,399
I wonder about something, Sofia.

353
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:52,199
You aren't messing with
Osman only for lands, I think.

354
00:35:56,090 --> 00:35:59,569
This is the hatred of years

355
00:36:00,680 --> 00:36:02,359
..Karesi Bey.

356
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,839
I won't stop until I take revenge.

357
00:36:08,680 --> 00:36:10,239
Don't you..

358
00:36:12,320 --> 00:36:15,519
..want Osman to die?

359
00:36:18,480 --> 00:36:21,119
Tell me where you stand.

360
00:36:21,920 --> 00:36:23,039
Against us?

361
00:36:24,480 --> 00:36:25,919
Or beside us?

362
00:36:27,960 --> 00:36:30,999
If you manage, I stand beside you.

363
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:33,679
If you fail

364
00:36:34,360 --> 00:36:38,119
...I will give you one more kick when you fall.

365
00:36:43,040 --> 00:36:45,519
Don't worry, Karesi Bey.

366
00:36:46,640 --> 00:36:50,319
Osman will kneel sooner or later.

367
00:36:53,240 --> 00:36:55,159
-Kanyumaz.
-My Bey.

368
00:36:56,200 --> 00:36:59,399
-Two horses.
-As you order, my Bey.

369
00:37:11,920 --> 00:37:18,279
-Well... Have a safe journey.
-Thanks, Karesi Bey.

370
00:37:36,080 --> 00:37:38,639
Clear the way!

371
00:37:39,760 --> 00:37:42,719
Come on, Bayhan Bey! Ride to the healing house!

372
00:37:46,760 --> 00:37:48,519
Come on!

373
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:55,119
Saruca! Saruca!

374
00:37:56,640 --> 00:37:58,399
My Allah..

375
00:37:59,760 --> 00:38:07,839
My son... My child! What
did they do to you, son?

376
00:38:09,520 --> 00:38:11,399
-Come on.
-Grab him.

377
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:14,159
Hazal Hatun.

378
00:38:16,840 --> 00:38:19,719
-Come on. I got him.
-Come on.

379
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:22,039
-My son!
-Come on!

380
00:38:24,400 --> 00:38:26,079
Come on!

381
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:31,279
Couldn't you save my son, husband?

382
00:38:32,680 --> 00:38:34,759
My Saruca!

383
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:43,359
Hazal Hatun.

384
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:47,199
-Hazal Hatun. Hey!
-Don't do this, Hazal Hatun.

385
00:38:47,360 --> 00:38:50,319
Alaaddin will take care
of him. He'll be alright.

386
00:38:50,320 --> 00:38:51,839
Dastards.

387
00:38:55,560 --> 00:38:58,959
-He'll be alright. -Of course he will.

388
00:38:59,080 --> 00:39:02,639
He will be alright. Saruca...

389
00:39:02,760 --> 00:39:06,079
Come on, Saruca -Sisters!

390
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:08,399
My son.

391
00:39:12,560 --> 00:39:14,559
Alps!

392
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:17,199
Those jackal won't stop, obviously.

393
00:39:17,600 --> 00:39:21,159
Increase the number of
patrols and hold the gates.

394
00:39:21,240 --> 00:39:24,479
Everybody! You all keep your eyes wide open!

395
00:39:24,800 --> 00:39:28,839
Only the members of this tribe will be let in.

396
00:39:28,880 --> 00:39:30,279
Come on.

397
00:39:31,480 --> 00:39:34,199
Orhan, what happened?

398
00:39:34,240 --> 00:39:36,159
Fatma? Is everybody alright?

399
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:38,079
They're good, Holofira.

400
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:40,799
Thank Allah, they are fine.

401
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:43,319
Those heathens' plan got ruined.

402
00:39:43,520 --> 00:39:47,879
Our land Sogut became their graveyard.

403
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:56,119
We sacrificed neither our
lives nor our fatherland Sogut!

404
00:39:56,280 --> 00:39:57,679
Now it's time..

405
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,719
...to make those vile dogs...

406
00:40:01,080 --> 00:40:05,679
...pay for harming our
property and making us bleed

407
00:40:05,720 --> 00:40:09,119
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

408
00:40:32,080 --> 00:40:35,079
Karesiogullari Beylic

409
00:40:38,560 --> 00:40:42,759
It seems Osman Bey made a great plan.

410
00:40:43,560 --> 00:40:46,999
I thought he would surrender
Sogut to the heathens.

411
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:52,559
What's your dilemma, Gencer Bey?

412
00:40:54,200 --> 00:40:56,879
Are you still thinking about Osman?

413
00:41:02,120 --> 00:41:03,479
Never!

414
00:41:03,960 --> 00:41:08,639
Osman Bey scolds me before
the other beys as if I were a kid!

415
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:14,399
Yet I joined many battles
and killed countless heathens!

416
00:41:15,960 --> 00:41:19,319
I wasn't born yesterday.

417
00:41:19,880 --> 00:41:22,279
I didn't deserve this, Karesi Bey.

418
00:41:23,240 --> 00:41:25,199
This is the spirit.

419
00:41:25,760 --> 00:41:27,999
Keep your anger alive.

420
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:33,879
Everybody will leave Osman
who never respects the morals.

421
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:39,559
My Bey is you.

422
00:41:40,360 --> 00:41:46,799
I always stand with the one who
respects the morals and rules with justice.

423
00:41:48,920 --> 00:41:50,759
Thank you, Gencer Bey.

424
00:41:51,640 --> 00:41:52,919
Thank you.

425
00:41:53,960 --> 00:41:55,639
Sancar.

426
00:42:04,120 --> 00:42:05,879
Well..

427
00:42:07,520 --> 00:42:09,679
Then..

428
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:14,999
...let's seal our alliance with a gift.

429
00:42:27,880 --> 00:42:29,799
Thank you, Karesi Bey.

430
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:36,439
I will always keep it.

431
00:42:39,560 --> 00:42:44,319
Now... Listen to me carefully.

432
00:42:45,840 --> 00:42:53,239
I want you to act like one of
Osman's beys, stay with him...

433
00:42:53,720 --> 00:42:58,199
...and keep me informed about everything.

434
00:42:59,400 --> 00:43:01,279
Why, Karesi Bey?

435
00:43:01,680 --> 00:43:05,599
To conquer Osman from the inside.

436
00:43:23,720 --> 00:43:26,159
Your anger is like a mountain, Osman.

437
00:43:26,640 --> 00:43:28,239
I can see that.

438
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:31,639
Karesi and his collaborators...

439
00:43:32,680 --> 00:43:35,079
I will put out their fires!

440
00:43:37,080 --> 00:43:38,959
Thanks, my Bala.

441
00:43:40,360 --> 00:43:42,079
Thanks.

442
00:43:47,280 --> 00:43:48,959
Do I have permission?

443
00:43:50,920 --> 00:43:53,159
Come in, Ayse Hatun.

444
00:44:00,880 --> 00:44:02,799
Osman Bey.

445
00:44:06,760 --> 00:44:08,639
Yes, Ayse Hatun?

446
00:44:09,240 --> 00:44:13,519
Do you have something to tell me?

447
00:44:16,960 --> 00:44:19,039
I can see it.

448
00:44:19,640 --> 00:44:22,599
You need to tell me something. Come here.

449
00:44:23,400 --> 00:44:24,879
Come closer to me.

450
00:44:27,280 --> 00:44:32,439
Come. Speak now.

451
00:44:33,760 --> 00:44:41,239
My father, Ilbay has been on duty for our
state, our state and you for a long time.

452
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:44,399
And?

453
00:44:44,960 --> 00:44:46,319
Are you..

454
00:44:47,040 --> 00:44:49,079
..angry with me for that?

455
00:44:49,440 --> 00:44:52,039
I'm not angry but proud.

456
00:44:52,280 --> 00:44:55,719
He's gone for you and our land.

457
00:44:56,720 --> 00:44:59,799
But Allah is my witness I miss him so much.

458
00:45:01,360 --> 00:45:03,239
But I don't tell anyone.

459
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:06,759
I cry only when I'm alone in my tent.

460
00:45:06,960 --> 00:45:09,279
Nobody should see me weak.

461
00:45:10,120 --> 00:45:12,199
My father taught me so.

462
00:45:13,240 --> 00:45:17,159
Oh... Ayse Hatun.

463
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:20,559
Your father taught you well.

464
00:45:22,720 --> 00:45:24,439
Then..

465
00:45:25,480 --> 00:45:27,799
Let me tell you this.

466
00:45:28,080 --> 00:45:31,919
Your father will be back in the tribe soon.

467
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:36,759
Your longing will be over.

468
00:45:37,160 --> 00:45:38,719
Don't be worrying.

469
00:45:44,120 --> 00:45:45,799
Oh...

470
00:45:51,200 --> 00:45:52,679
Fools.

471
00:45:55,840 --> 00:45:57,399
How?

472
00:45:58,760 --> 00:46:00,239
How?

473
00:46:00,960 --> 00:46:05,449
How could you lose her? How?

474
00:46:07,320 --> 00:46:11,839
Whoever caused this will
face a worse fate than death!

475
00:46:12,040 --> 00:46:16,119
Sir, Turks came to the gate
disguising as our soldiers.

476
00:46:17,800 --> 00:46:21,599
And these fools opened the gate
without questioning. Is that so?

477
00:46:22,320 --> 00:46:26,079
Prisoners escaped from the
dungeon before Turks came inside.

478
00:46:26,200 --> 00:46:29,759
Someone killed all the guards.
-So...

479
00:46:30,280 --> 00:46:32,599
There is a spy among us.

480
00:46:42,520 --> 00:46:45,439
You will find him, Hristo.

481
00:46:45,680 --> 00:46:49,839
You will find out who took my best leverage.

482
00:46:50,840 --> 00:46:54,199
Soldiers, come with me! Now!

483
00:47:02,040 --> 00:47:05,999
We'll definitely find Osman's rat, Lukas.

484
00:47:06,400 --> 00:47:07,879
I will find, Sofia.

485
00:47:08,040 --> 00:47:10,359
I will find and cut his breath.

486
00:47:12,840 --> 00:47:14,999
Your name is Sofia, huh?

487
00:47:20,400 --> 00:47:21,759
My son.

488
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:25,439
My boy. My Saruca..

489
00:47:32,520 --> 00:47:34,199
My Allah..

490
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:37,519
My Allah, take from my
life and give it to my son.

491
00:47:38,080 --> 00:47:40,119
I'd gladly accept that.

492
00:47:44,560 --> 00:47:46,759
Don't think of the bad.

493
00:47:47,800 --> 00:47:49,719
Our child will be alright.

494
00:47:54,720 --> 00:47:57,999
He will be alright. Won't he, Alaaddin Bey?

495
00:48:03,280 --> 00:48:06,919
I cleaned the wound well
and applied ointment on to it.

496
00:48:08,560 --> 00:48:09,879
But..

497
00:48:10,680 --> 00:48:12,679
Although I did my best

498
00:48:13,040 --> 00:48:14,239
..he bled too much.

499
00:48:15,640 --> 00:48:18,439
Molasses!

500
00:48:19,760 --> 00:48:23,039
I will bring molasses! My son should drink.

501
00:48:23,400 --> 00:48:26,199
Just pray for him, Hazal Hatun.

502
00:48:29,240 --> 00:48:31,639
He turned out to be stronger than he looked.

503
00:48:32,480 --> 00:48:34,239
He'll be alright, God willing.

504
00:48:34,280 --> 00:48:35,959
God willing.

505
00:48:40,760 --> 00:48:42,199
I hope he recovers.

506
00:48:42,320 --> 00:48:44,079
Thank you, Alaaddin Bey.

507
00:48:44,440 --> 00:48:47,559
-Thank you, thank you.
May Allah be pleased with you.

508
00:48:50,120 --> 00:48:52,039
My Allah..

509
00:48:57,680 --> 00:49:01,159
You protected my life with your life.

510
00:49:02,920 --> 00:49:05,119
Things I said to you earlier...

511
00:49:05,600 --> 00:49:07,919
...are piercing my heart now.

512
00:49:09,560 --> 00:49:11,399
Recover fast, Saruca.

513
00:49:12,040 --> 00:49:13,879
Recover fast.

514
00:49:14,560 --> 00:49:16,239
Don't leave us in sorrow.

515
00:49:25,960 --> 00:49:28,519
Right before everyone

516
00:49:28,680 --> 00:49:32,359
...before Fatma and all the beys, he slapped me!

517
00:49:32,560 --> 00:49:33,999
He slapped me!

518
00:49:34,480 --> 00:49:36,814
Calm down, Yusuf. He's the Bey.

519
00:49:36,826 --> 00:49:38,439
How can I calm down?

520
00:49:38,520 --> 00:49:41,319
I got disgraced before everyone!

521
00:49:41,360 --> 00:49:42,239
You didn't!

522
00:49:42,480 --> 00:49:45,319
You didn't, brother. He's the ruler of us.

523
00:49:46,400 --> 00:49:47,719
Look.

524
00:49:48,280 --> 00:49:49,119
Yusuf.

525
00:49:49,200 --> 00:49:52,519
You shouldn't be angry with
the slap your Bey gives you.

526
00:49:52,720 --> 00:49:54,519
You should just take a lesson.

527
00:49:54,800 --> 00:49:57,279
You made a mistake. You disobeyed...
-Sister!

528
00:50:00,400 --> 00:50:03,919
You don't feel disgraced
because you got slapped, Yusuf.

529
00:50:05,760 --> 00:50:08,519
Just because you got slapped before Fatma Hatun

530
00:50:10,760 --> 00:50:12,479
...you can't digest it.

531
00:50:15,520 --> 00:50:19,799
-I can't talk to Fatma anymore.
-You will.

532
00:50:21,400 --> 00:50:22,839
Yusuf.

533
00:50:23,600 --> 00:50:24,919
My brother.

534
00:50:25,280 --> 00:50:29,399
A man must stand up when he falls.

535
00:50:30,720 --> 00:50:32,559
You made a mistake.

536
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:35,399
And you paid a heavy price.

537
00:50:45,360 --> 00:50:46,959
Brother.
-Yes?

538
00:50:47,200 --> 00:50:49,239
I need to tell you something.

539
00:50:50,240 --> 00:50:52,839
From your eyes, I can see what you'll tell.

540
00:50:53,160 --> 00:50:54,519
But you speak.

541
00:50:54,640 --> 00:50:56,599
Let's see if I'm right.

542
00:51:10,520 --> 00:51:15,239
Brother... So far,
we have said nothing.

543
00:51:15,520 --> 00:51:20,119
We have always kept silent and
never questioned. But you see?

544
00:51:20,720 --> 00:51:22,319
Begum Hatun.

545
00:51:22,720 --> 00:51:26,359
She never stops making mistakes.

546
00:51:26,960 --> 00:51:28,679
This isn't going well.

547
00:51:31,000 --> 00:51:32,719
I know, brother.

548
00:51:34,040 --> 00:51:36,239
First Karadin, then Sogut...

549
00:51:36,720 --> 00:51:40,759
Wherever Begum Hatun touches, she damages us.

550
00:51:41,040 --> 00:51:42,399
I know.

551
00:51:42,760 --> 00:51:46,199
Well, brother... My brother
spoiled them too much.

552
00:51:48,760 --> 00:51:53,319
I've been thinking about how we can
tell our Bey about this, though.

553
00:51:54,120 --> 00:51:55,719
Not only her.

554
00:51:55,840 --> 00:51:58,359
Her brother as well.

555
00:51:58,440 --> 00:52:03,439
We trusted him for the caravan of the market.

556
00:52:03,840 --> 00:52:05,479
But he couldn't protect.

557
00:52:06,080 --> 00:52:07,519
Well, brother...

558
00:52:07,960 --> 00:52:10,439
Why do we even need them?

559
00:52:14,960 --> 00:52:16,959
He got only wounded this time.

560
00:52:17,040 --> 00:52:22,079
If he dies next time, everything will be worse.

561
00:52:22,920 --> 00:52:26,239
She and her brother are harming us, Cerkutay.

562
00:52:27,840 --> 00:52:30,319
But how can we tell our Bey about this?

563
00:52:30,600 --> 00:52:34,519
You think he can't see it?
You think we should show him?

564
00:52:34,680 --> 00:52:36,999
What are we for, brother?

565
00:52:37,400 --> 00:52:41,199
Why do we stand beside our Bey?

566
00:52:42,240 --> 00:52:45,239
This isn't even questioning.

567
00:52:45,560 --> 00:52:48,359
This is telling the truth.

568
00:52:49,840 --> 00:52:52,759
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

569
00:52:52,840 --> 00:52:55,079
Cerkutay Bey. Boran Bey.

570
00:52:55,360 --> 00:52:59,319
-A meeting will be held shortly.
-Okay, Aykurt Cavus.

571
00:52:59,440 --> 00:53:00,679
Okay, thanks.

572
00:53:02,800 --> 00:53:04,599
Let's go.

573
00:53:10,640 --> 00:53:14,159
While I thought Osman Bey
would surrender Sogut to the enemy,

574
00:53:14,560 --> 00:53:18,799
...Osman Bey had other plans.

575
00:53:20,520 --> 00:53:25,359
Have you ever seen Osman Bey
acting without measures, Gencer Bey?

576
00:53:30,800 --> 00:53:34,799
-Attention! Osman Bey!
-Peace be upon you.

577
00:53:34,800 --> 00:53:36,319
Peace be upon you, too.

578
00:53:41,840 --> 00:53:43,879
Sit down.

579
00:53:50,880 --> 00:53:53,559
We have..

580
00:53:53,560 --> 00:53:57,239
...informed our enemies
once again of our morals...

581
00:53:58,800 --> 00:54:01,799
...and made them understand
that even for our lives...

582
00:54:02,320 --> 00:54:06,079
...we will never give up
even a piece of our land.

583
00:54:07,240 --> 00:54:10,418
We fight for the Name of
The Righteous, my Bey.

584
00:54:10,430 --> 00:54:13,759
We will succeed in both worlds,
with Allah's permission.

585
00:54:13,760 --> 00:54:16,999
Right. Right.

586
00:54:18,530 --> 00:54:20,359
We know our enemies.

587
00:54:20,720 --> 00:54:21,959
Lukas on one side.

588
00:54:23,480 --> 00:54:27,799
And that Hatun named Veronica on the other.

589
00:54:29,480 --> 00:54:31,119
And Karesi Bey who saved...

590
00:54:32,240 --> 00:54:35,879
...them from our swords on the other side.

591
00:54:38,560 --> 00:54:40,159
If we are going to take lives...

592
00:54:41,200 --> 00:54:45,119
...killing that Lukas dog is the
most important for me, my Bey.

593
00:54:46,440 --> 00:54:51,239
Your revenge is our revenge. But...

594
00:54:52,040 --> 00:54:54,479
...there is something we need to do first.

595
00:54:56,000 --> 00:54:58,199
For us..

596
00:55:00,280 --> 00:55:01,599
...there is a huge danger...

597
00:55:03,680 --> 00:55:06,319
...and that is the snake who hides her face.

598
00:55:11,800 --> 00:55:15,279
Now, tell me, what should we do...

599
00:55:15,960 --> 00:55:19,159
...to make them pay for what they did?

600
00:55:21,160 --> 00:55:23,239
I suggest we follow Lukas, my Bey.

601
00:55:23,480 --> 00:55:25,759
After all, they are always together.

602
00:55:26,480 --> 00:55:30,079
The moment they leave the
castle, we will attack them.

603
00:55:31,680 --> 00:55:33,399
Gencer Bey.

604
00:55:33,960 --> 00:55:36,839
Tell me, what should we
do without losing our men?

605
00:55:37,400 --> 00:55:39,639
My path will require losses, my Bey.

606
00:55:39,880 --> 00:55:45,239
Once they have no captives for them to hide
behind, we can go and surround Akhisar again.

607
00:55:46,080 --> 00:55:47,679
Let's kill them all my Bey!

608
00:55:54,160 --> 00:55:57,719
Begum Hatun...
What is your opinion?

609
00:55:59,720 --> 00:56:03,839
We should do what they
did to Fatma Hatun, my Bey.

610
00:56:05,200 --> 00:56:09,519
Let's disguise ourselves and confront
her at her most vulnerable moment.

611
00:56:10,080 --> 00:56:11,919
What do you say, Cerkutay?

612
00:56:16,960 --> 00:56:18,119
Cerkutay Bey

613
00:56:20,880 --> 00:56:23,359
What do you think?

614
00:56:23,760 --> 00:56:25,439
My Bey...

615
00:56:29,360 --> 00:56:31,039
Whatever path..

616
00:56:31,840 --> 00:56:34,199
..is most suitable for you..

617
00:56:34,200 --> 00:56:36,919
..I will follow it.

618
00:56:54,240 --> 00:56:57,239
And what about the others, the other suspects?

619
00:56:57,680 --> 00:56:59,439
What do we know about them?

620
00:56:59,480 --> 00:57:02,839
Helen has just arrived, but she is too curious.

621
00:57:03,560 --> 00:57:05,759
The other one is the new groom.

622
00:57:06,240 --> 00:57:07,279
Groom?

623
00:57:10,360 --> 00:57:11,679
When did he come?

624
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:15,439
Our horses in the castle
were all infected by a disease.

625
00:57:15,800 --> 00:57:19,039
He came around that time.
He knows a lot about horses.

626
00:57:19,880 --> 00:57:22,799
Keep an eye on them. But be careful.

627
00:57:23,360 --> 00:57:25,279
They must not notice. -Yes sir.

628
00:57:29,560 --> 00:57:32,119
Osman is celebrating his victory now.

629
00:57:32,800 --> 00:57:34,879
But..

630
00:57:36,400 --> 00:57:38,919
...I will hit him at his weakest part.

631
00:57:43,600 --> 00:57:45,359
Bala.

632
00:57:47,400 --> 00:57:48,679
Bala.

633
00:57:50,440 --> 00:57:52,399
What is on your mind, Sofia?

634
00:57:53,000 --> 00:57:57,439
They have increased security on
all the roads from Sogut to the tribe.

635
00:57:57,600 --> 00:57:59,639
They know Veronica now as well.

636
00:57:59,760 --> 00:58:02,079
You cannot go to the marketplace as well.

637
00:58:02,080 --> 00:58:04,839
They will take the caravan out tomorrow.

638
00:58:05,320 --> 00:58:09,639
There are difficult paths
to defend on the route.

639
00:58:10,640 --> 00:58:13,399
When Bala is in Sogut, we will raid the caravan.

640
00:58:14,640 --> 00:58:19,064
And when Bala hears the
news, she will fall into our trap...

641
00:58:19,076 --> 00:58:21,039
...to protect the caravan.

642
00:58:22,120 --> 00:58:23,719
Ah Sofia!

643
00:58:24,760 --> 00:58:26,199
Your mind has no limits.

644
00:58:26,200 --> 00:58:29,399
Osman will give anything for Bala, everything.

645
00:58:30,800 --> 00:58:33,319
But this time, there will be no bargaining.

646
00:58:34,520 --> 00:58:36,159
Only death.

647
00:58:37,480 --> 00:58:41,319
First Bala, then Osman.

648
00:58:41,320 --> 00:58:43,079
I will take both of their lives.

649
00:58:45,480 --> 00:58:49,839
I will kill them not just
once, but a thousand times.

650
00:58:51,760 --> 00:58:53,639
What's on your mind, Sofia?

651
00:58:59,920 --> 00:59:01,599
Before I kill Bala..

652
00:59:03,000 --> 00:59:05,799
...I will tell her such a secret that...

653
00:59:11,720 --> 00:59:15,079
...she will die a thousand times.

654
00:59:24,080 --> 00:59:28,479
I need to get out of here quickly and
tell that woman's name to Osman Bey.

655
00:59:28,600 --> 00:59:31,279
Come on, my boy.

656
00:59:37,040 --> 00:59:39,639
Are you going somewhere?

657
00:59:48,480 --> 00:59:51,239
I put new horseshoes on the horses, sir.

658
00:59:51,240 --> 00:59:53,970
I was going to test
them in the fields.

659
00:59:53,982 --> 00:59:55,119
There's no rush.

660
00:59:55,720 --> 00:59:58,759
The Turks' watchmen might be around the castle.

661
01:00:01,200 --> 01:00:04,839
I'm not afraid of them sir.
-You are brave.

662
01:00:05,240 --> 01:00:09,479
But you have more important
duties than riding horses in the fields.

663
01:00:10,240 --> 01:00:13,439
Until tomorrow, you will
check all the horses in Akhisar.

664
01:00:13,560 --> 01:00:17,839
You will identify all sick horses
that are not ready for the way.

665
01:00:18,320 --> 01:00:19,959
Soldiers!

666
01:00:23,280 --> 01:00:26,119
Soldiers will be with you until you are done.

667
01:00:26,120 --> 01:00:28,999
They will help you.

668
01:00:46,040 --> 01:00:49,839
First Baysungur and his men,
and then Fatma and the others.

669
01:00:51,040 --> 01:00:57,239
My Bey, that Hatun named Veronica clearly
wants something more than our lands.

670
01:00:58,360 --> 01:00:59,719
Every step she takes...

671
01:00:59,920 --> 01:01:03,599
...every move she makes,
she tries to hurt us even more.

672
01:01:07,480 --> 01:01:09,679
Her intention is..

673
01:01:10,360 --> 01:01:12,719
..to hurt me first.

674
01:01:16,080 --> 01:01:20,079
When she went to the market,
she went with her face uncovered.

675
01:01:20,360 --> 01:01:26,519
But when she was facing
me, she covered her face.

676
01:01:27,680 --> 01:01:31,679
She said she would only show her face to me
while killing me.

677
01:01:34,800 --> 01:01:36,159
Good then.

678
01:01:36,440 --> 01:01:39,559
So that she wants to kill me so much...

679
01:01:41,120 --> 01:01:42,879
..let's give her a chance.

680
01:01:44,360 --> 01:01:46,559
What are you thinking, Osman Bey?

681
01:01:46,600 --> 01:01:48,079
Karesi Bey..

682
01:01:50,680 --> 01:01:53,759
...wanted to turn these
lands into a hunting ground.

683
01:01:53,760 --> 01:01:57,399
He wanted to hunt infidels together.

684
01:02:05,240 --> 01:02:06,959
Two faced Karesi Bey.

685
01:02:08,800 --> 01:02:10,159
-Boran.
-My Bey.

686
01:02:11,040 --> 01:02:13,399
Send news to Karesi Bey.

687
01:02:13,400 --> 01:02:14,799
I am...

688
01:02:16,760 --> 01:02:18,599
...inviting him to my hunt.

689
01:02:19,080 --> 01:02:21,039
Yes my Bey.

690
01:02:22,720 --> 01:02:24,719
Now Karesi Bey...

691
01:02:24,720 --> 01:02:27,159
..will do his best to secure..

692
01:02:28,800 --> 01:02:30,599
..his alliance with infidels.

693
01:02:31,640 --> 01:02:34,839
First, he will mention
about the hunt to his friends.

694
01:02:35,400 --> 01:02:38,559
What do you want to
achieve with this plan, my Bey?

695
01:02:38,560 --> 01:02:40,439
Now our goal will be this.

696
01:02:41,400 --> 01:02:48,079
When he tells his allies about the hunting
place, they will think we will fall into a trap.

697
01:02:49,640 --> 01:02:53,039
Veronica will come there.

698
01:02:53,040 --> 01:02:57,999
Then Veronica will be in our hands.

699
01:03:05,560 --> 01:03:08,119
Boran, Cerkutay.
Tomorrow, at Gundogan...

700
01:03:08,800 --> 01:03:12,279
...you will go to the places
we will hunt and set the traps.

701
01:03:12,280 --> 01:03:15,319
But you will take all the precautions.

702
01:03:16,440 --> 01:03:18,039
Yes my Bey.

703
01:03:20,560 --> 01:03:21,959
You can leave.

704
01:03:43,200 --> 01:03:45,239
What happened, Beys?

705
01:03:45,240 --> 01:03:47,359
Do you have something to say?

706
01:04:01,800 --> 01:04:03,559
My Bey...

707
01:04:04,360 --> 01:04:07,319
We are not sure if we will
have gone too far, but...

708
01:04:07,560 --> 01:04:10,359
...there's an issue that makes us concerned.

709
01:04:11,800 --> 01:04:13,319
My Bey, we...

710
01:04:13,880 --> 01:04:16,679
...couldn't say that at the council but...
-You had to!

711
01:04:20,240 --> 01:04:23,119
If this is about the council..

712
01:04:24,040 --> 01:04:25,599
You had to speak...

713
01:04:27,680 --> 01:04:29,559
...when I gave you the chance.

714
01:04:34,840 --> 01:04:37,279
The council is over.

715
01:04:37,280 --> 01:04:39,279
Now it's time to hunt.

716
01:04:40,880 --> 01:04:42,679
Now..

717
01:04:43,520 --> 01:04:45,439
Go and do your duties.

718
01:04:47,280 --> 01:04:49,759
-Yes my Bey.
-Yes my Bey.

719
01:05:04,360 --> 01:05:05,879
You called me Bala Hatun.

720
01:05:06,560 --> 01:05:09,919
You came together with your
brother, right, Begum Hatun?

721
01:05:09,960 --> 01:05:11,769
Yes, thanks to Allah.

722
01:05:12,840 --> 01:05:16,479
Thanks to Osman Bey, Sogut
and our children are saved.

723
01:05:17,080 --> 01:05:18,519
Good.

724
01:05:18,960 --> 01:05:20,759
Now it is time to answer.

725
01:05:22,240 --> 01:05:24,719
I know I cannot make up for my mistake.

726
01:05:24,720 --> 01:05:27,879
Knowing it does not change anything, Begum.

727
01:05:28,160 --> 01:05:31,079
There is no compensation for this mistake.

728
01:05:31,360 --> 01:05:36,239
Do you allow people to trade in our
marketplace without questioning them?

729
01:05:36,600 --> 01:05:40,519
Didn't you investigate before
letting that devil into the market?

730
01:05:40,520 --> 01:05:42,119
I did, of course, Bala Hatun.

731
01:05:42,480 --> 01:05:43,879
But no one knew her.

732
01:05:43,880 --> 01:05:46,919
I sent Alps around and I was
waiting for them to inform me.

733
01:05:47,000 --> 01:05:48,719
No one knew her.

734
01:05:51,480 --> 01:05:54,239
While you were waiting for news...

735
01:05:54,240 --> 01:05:56,519
..that devil abducted my child, Begum!

736
01:05:59,680 --> 01:06:03,159
From the marketplace you were
watching over and protecting.

737
01:06:04,280 --> 01:06:07,207
Am I the only one at fault, Bala
Hatun? My brother was also..

738
01:06:07,219 --> 01:06:08,199
Shut up!

739
01:06:08,200 --> 01:06:10,999
Don't look for someone else
to blame for your mistake.

740
01:06:11,000 --> 01:06:13,119
You let that devil into the marketplace.

741
01:06:13,120 --> 01:06:15,319
And you will pay the price.

742
01:06:15,320 --> 01:06:19,639
If I have to pay a price, I will.

743
01:06:20,440 --> 01:06:23,279
We gave you a duty to make up for your mistake.

744
01:06:24,080 --> 01:06:25,839
And you failed that as well.

745
01:06:26,800 --> 01:06:28,519
But I will talk to Osman Bey.

746
01:06:29,200 --> 01:06:30,559
I will dismiss you.

747
01:06:32,560 --> 01:06:34,999
Know that.

748
01:07:28,760 --> 01:07:30,919
Gunkurt.

749
01:07:34,120 --> 01:07:35,639
My Bey.

750
01:07:36,120 --> 01:07:39,999
Take this to Karesi without letting them notice.

751
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:41,839
Yes my Bey.

752
01:07:45,400 --> 01:07:49,759
Learning Osman's move
will be very useful for Karesi.

753
01:08:13,520 --> 01:08:15,519
Osman.

754
01:08:17,279 --> 01:08:19,319
Ah Osman.

755
01:08:21,040 --> 01:08:22,879
If it wasn't for my love for you...

756
01:08:24,960 --> 01:08:27,399
...I would set this tribe on fire..

757
01:08:27,760 --> 01:08:29,639
...and show that Bala her place.

758
01:08:33,520 --> 01:08:35,118
But...

759
01:08:35,120 --> 01:08:37,359
..you don't see me..

760
01:08:37,359 --> 01:08:40,037
..and you don't see my love.

761
01:08:42,399 --> 01:08:49,037
Like the dagger I've carried for years,
the love I've carried with forty locks.

762
01:08:50,760 --> 01:08:55,037
My Allah..

763
01:08:55,920 --> 01:08:57,559
If giving up was possible...

764
01:09:00,720 --> 01:09:02,319
But no...

765
01:09:02,760 --> 01:09:04,799
I can't..

766
01:09:05,319 --> 01:09:06,719
Giving up on my love...

767
01:09:07,720 --> 01:09:12,319
...is giving up on my life!

768
01:09:12,319 --> 01:09:13,399
Bala...

769
01:09:14,479 --> 01:09:16,999
Despite you..

770
01:09:18,479 --> 01:09:21,599
I won't give up on Osman.

771
01:10:03,120 --> 01:10:04,799
Gonca.

772
01:10:05,160 --> 01:10:06,919
Are you alright? What happened?

773
01:10:07,320 --> 01:10:09,639
Aunt, you seem pale.

774
01:10:09,640 --> 01:10:11,839
Did you receive bad news?

775
01:10:11,840 --> 01:10:14,999
No, no my Fatma. I am alright.

776
01:10:16,560 --> 01:10:18,119
What are you doing here?

777
01:10:19,160 --> 01:10:21,679
I was telling my brother how I escaped.

778
01:10:23,960 --> 01:10:26,159
Brother...
Alright. Alright. Tell her.

779
01:10:26,840 --> 01:10:30,679
-Do you want me to tell you as well?
-Yes my Fatma.

780
01:10:32,480 --> 01:10:38,359
We ran away and then..

781
01:10:39,040 --> 01:10:40,039
...they saved us...

782
01:10:40,040 --> 01:10:42,799
...they said "Wear the clothes
of Byzantium soldiers"...

783
01:10:42,800 --> 01:10:45,599
...then we fought and
killed them with our swords...

784
01:10:48,520 --> 01:10:53,239
That woman has a problem with us.

785
01:10:53,240 --> 01:10:54,799
So, she won't stop.

786
01:10:54,800 --> 01:10:57,799
My Bala, everyone in the tribe will be cautious.

787
01:10:58,320 --> 01:11:00,479
You too.

788
01:11:00,480 --> 01:11:02,559
But most importantly, my Fatma.

789
01:11:03,440 --> 01:11:05,159
Don't worry, my Bey.

790
01:11:05,160 --> 01:11:06,359
I will take care of it.

791
01:11:07,120 --> 01:11:09,639
I will give Fatma a duty in the tribe.

792
01:11:10,160 --> 01:11:11,999
Okay, okay, okay.

793
01:11:12,800 --> 01:11:15,359
We must also please the people of Sogut.

794
01:11:17,640 --> 01:11:21,159
Orhan, this task is yours, my son.
-Yes my Bey.

795
01:11:21,160 --> 01:11:24,919
I will think about what needs
to be done for the people.

796
01:11:26,160 --> 01:11:27,599
Actually...

797
01:11:27,800 --> 01:11:32,639
The goods that we keep in the storehouse,
which Karesi Bey wanted to take from us...

798
01:11:32,720 --> 01:11:35,439
Can't we trade them in the Sogut market?

799
01:11:35,440 --> 01:11:40,399
It will increase the trade,
and the people will be happy.

800
01:11:44,080 --> 01:11:50,639
You've thought well, my daughter.

801
01:11:50,640 --> 01:11:52,799
She thought well, my Bala.

802
01:11:52,800 --> 01:11:55,239
Then, this duty is yours.

803
01:11:55,550 --> 01:11:56,919
Mine.

804
01:11:58,280 --> 01:12:01,759
So, where is Alaeddin? Where is my Fatma?

805
01:12:02,720 --> 01:12:05,919
My Bey, Fatma took Alaeddin and Gonca captive.

806
01:12:05,920 --> 01:12:07,679
They will come soon.

807
01:12:12,200 --> 01:12:15,159
-Yes?
-That's right.

808
01:12:15,320 --> 01:12:17,799
I put the sword in and ran away.

809
01:12:17,880 --> 01:12:20,639
Alright, sister.
Alright, dear sister.

810
01:12:20,640 --> 01:12:22,199
You told me three times.

811
01:12:22,200 --> 01:12:23,679
I really got it.

812
01:12:23,720 --> 01:12:26,439
Hey, don't be so impatient.

813
01:12:26,440 --> 01:12:29,079
My daughter, come here. Come.

814
01:12:29,560 --> 01:12:31,119
Tell me about it.

815
01:12:31,520 --> 01:12:33,199
Don't do this, father.

816
01:12:33,600 --> 01:12:35,959
She's been telling the same story for an hour.

817
01:12:36,160 --> 01:12:38,159
Stop talking.

818
01:12:38,680 --> 01:12:40,239
You keep quiet.

819
01:12:41,080 --> 01:12:43,279
What happened there, daughter?

820
01:12:44,600 --> 01:12:45,679
Father.

821
01:12:46,160 --> 01:12:50,079
My brothers envy me.

822
01:12:54,360 --> 01:12:56,119
That's why they are doing this.

823
01:12:56,560 --> 01:12:59,519
I proved myself.

824
01:13:00,520 --> 01:13:03,879
-I can join the battles, right?
-No battles for you.

825
01:13:04,840 --> 01:13:06,359
Why would you?

826
01:13:06,680 --> 01:13:09,079
You will just sit by me.

827
01:13:09,640 --> 01:13:12,399
You will always stick with us.

828
01:13:12,600 --> 01:13:16,199
No more going to the market place either.
-Mother.

829
01:13:22,000 --> 01:13:24,079
No battles!

830
01:13:25,160 --> 01:13:27,439
Father.

831
01:13:36,200 --> 01:13:37,679
Mother.

832
01:13:38,360 --> 01:13:40,239
Speaking of the market...

833
01:13:42,480 --> 01:13:44,399
Gonca has an idea.

834
01:13:45,760 --> 01:13:49,879
Right. My sister-in-saw has
a great idea. Tell them, sister.

835
01:13:50,840 --> 01:13:53,239
No battles. You speak, my girl.

836
01:13:54,720 --> 01:13:59,399
Father, what about putting the
goods in the store in the market?

837
01:14:08,680 --> 01:14:12,039
You see how hard your
daughter-in-laws work, Osman Bey?

838
01:14:15,080 --> 01:14:18,239
My dear, Holofira just said the same thing.

839
01:14:21,760 --> 01:14:23,879
We assigned her.

840
01:14:37,680 --> 01:14:39,199
Well..

841
01:14:40,720 --> 01:14:42,679
You tell me, dear.

842
01:14:43,120 --> 01:14:45,159
How did you escape from the carriage?

843
01:14:45,360 --> 01:14:46,999
Oh no, my Bey.

844
01:14:50,800 --> 01:14:53,399
Don't do this, father.

845
01:14:53,760 --> 01:14:56,439
Are you still talking? Tell me, dear.

846
01:14:57,480 --> 01:14:58,799
Father.

847
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:01,159
-Well...
-Hmm..

848
01:15:01,600 --> 01:15:04,599
Karesiogullari Beylic

849
01:15:05,040 --> 01:15:10,479
Osman Bey invites us to the hunt tomorrow, huh?

850
01:15:13,480 --> 01:15:14,839
Sancar.

851
01:15:15,440 --> 01:15:19,119
He's up to something, but...

852
01:15:20,520 --> 01:15:23,639
Osman Bey can't make a plan against you, my Bey.

853
01:15:23,840 --> 01:15:26,599
If he does, he'll be the one to be hunted.

854
01:15:27,640 --> 01:15:33,399
The wolf sees the lion as a
prey not because he's brave...

855
01:15:34,480 --> 01:15:36,759
..but because he's blind.

856
01:15:38,000 --> 01:15:39,679
Do I have permission, my Bey?

857
01:15:40,000 --> 01:15:41,999
Come in, Kanyumaz.

858
01:15:47,280 --> 01:15:50,119
My Bey, I've brought a note from Gencer Bey.

859
01:16:00,200 --> 01:16:07,839
Osman Bey knows that Lukas and the
woman with him escaped with your help.

860
01:16:08,720 --> 01:16:16,239
And he thinks you will let them
know about his invitation for you.

861
01:16:16,920 --> 01:16:23,199
While they attempt to kill Osman Bey
when he's unprotected during the hunt

862
01:16:23,720 --> 01:16:27,279
...Osman Bey will hunt them.

863
01:16:36,720 --> 01:16:38,519
Osman.

864
01:16:40,600 --> 01:16:44,799
You think you are smart.

865
01:16:46,040 --> 01:16:51,119
But I'm always a step ahead of you.

866
01:16:54,760 --> 01:16:56,559
-Sancar.
-Yes, my Bey?

867
01:16:57,000 --> 01:16:59,039
Inform Osman Bey...

868
01:17:00,080 --> 01:17:02,999
...that I'm accepting his invitation.

869
01:17:03,160 --> 01:17:04,959
As you order, my Bey.

870
01:17:10,040 --> 01:17:13,119
Bala, just spill the beans.

871
01:17:14,080 --> 01:17:15,999
Begum Hatun, my Bey.

872
01:17:19,400 --> 01:17:24,039
She made many mistakes in
Karadin and we forgave her.

873
01:17:25,080 --> 01:17:28,839
She acted impertinently and we tolerated.

874
01:17:29,560 --> 01:17:34,319
We gave her a duty in the marketplace of
Sogut because she had weak ties with us.

875
01:17:34,520 --> 01:17:36,439
But she failed.

876
01:17:37,400 --> 01:17:42,119
We've seen what her failure cost.

877
01:17:43,080 --> 01:17:44,559
Of course.

878
01:17:45,680 --> 01:17:49,359
I'm thinking about a suitable
punishment for her failure.

879
01:17:50,360 --> 01:17:54,439
I don't want to
punish her, but...

880
01:17:54,640 --> 01:17:57,039
...someone good should take over her duty.

881
01:17:58,160 --> 01:18:01,439
I think we should dismiss Begum Hatun, my Bey.

882
01:18:04,720 --> 01:18:06,719
Do you have someone in your mind?

883
01:18:07,000 --> 01:18:08,359
Yes.

884
01:18:10,160 --> 01:18:11,999
Do I have permission, my Bey?

885
01:18:14,480 --> 01:18:15,959
Come in.

886
01:18:18,440 --> 01:18:21,599
My Bey, Begum Hatun is
here. She wants to see you.

887
01:18:22,640 --> 01:18:24,039
Let her in.

888
01:18:36,120 --> 01:18:37,599
Speak, Begum Hatun.

889
01:18:38,000 --> 01:18:43,079
As you came at this hour, you must
have something important to say, huh?

890
01:18:44,480 --> 01:18:45,519
Yes.

891
01:18:50,880 --> 01:18:52,239
Osman Bey.

892
01:18:53,720 --> 01:18:59,759
First, I want you to know that I'm loyal
to you and your cause until my last day.

893
01:19:00,440 --> 01:19:02,479
My loyalty will never end.

894
01:19:02,920 --> 01:19:04,439
Thank you, Begum Hatun.

895
01:19:07,160 --> 01:19:08,799
But..

896
01:19:09,400 --> 01:19:12,359
I made a mistake during the
kidnapping of Fatma Hatun.

897
01:19:15,520 --> 01:19:17,199
With your permission

898
01:19:17,680 --> 01:19:20,799
...I'd like to be dismissed
from my duty on the market.

899
01:19:21,280 --> 01:19:24,959
And I want no other duties
but having conquests with you.

900
01:19:35,040 --> 01:19:37,679
You will keep your duty on the market.

901
01:19:42,360 --> 01:19:44,639
I'm not dismissing you.

902
01:19:49,200 --> 01:19:54,239
Don't ask me for any other duties...

903
01:19:56,680 --> 01:19:58,959
...or dismissal from your current duty.

904
01:20:02,080 --> 01:20:03,719
You may leave.

905
01:20:05,000 --> 01:20:06,959
Whatever you order, Osman Bey.

906
01:20:25,280 --> 01:20:28,239
You don't want to dismiss her, my Bey.

907
01:20:28,400 --> 01:20:30,599
So you must have a plan, huh?

908
01:20:31,280 --> 01:20:32,799
This is a duty of the state.

909
01:20:35,960 --> 01:20:38,519
Nobody can change it at their wills.

910
01:20:47,920 --> 01:20:49,239
Look.

911
01:20:49,560 --> 01:20:51,479
You got worried for nothing.

912
01:20:53,360 --> 01:20:56,679
You pulled your beautiful
face for nothing, Holofira.

913
01:21:01,000 --> 01:21:02,999
I'm trying to stay strong.

914
01:21:04,080 --> 01:21:06,039
But I can't help it, Orhan.

915
01:21:06,880 --> 01:21:08,519
I got scared.

916
01:21:08,920 --> 01:21:10,279
Fatma told me..

917
01:21:10,920 --> 01:21:13,159
The arrow almost...
-The arrow...

918
01:21:15,440 --> 01:21:17,599
..hit the talisman, Holofira.

919
01:21:22,400 --> 01:21:25,159
It hit the talisman you put around my neck.

920
01:21:25,840 --> 01:21:28,879
Look. I didn't get
wounded at all.

921
01:21:29,760 --> 01:21:32,639
But the talisman... It got destroyed.

922
01:21:37,440 --> 01:21:40,399
Never mind. It protected you.

923
01:21:42,160 --> 01:21:44,279
Allah protected me, Holofira.

924
01:21:44,720 --> 01:21:47,799
He protected me through you and this talisman.

925
01:21:48,840 --> 01:21:50,919
Let's see what's written inside.

926
01:22:00,120 --> 01:22:02,769
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

927
01:22:02,834 --> 01:22:09,194
“Allah alone is sufficient as an aid for us and
He is the best Protector.” [Al Imran Surah 173]

928
01:22:11,920 --> 01:22:13,519
What does that mean?

929
01:22:13,920 --> 01:22:15,679
It's written in an Qur'an.

930
01:22:16,200 --> 01:22:17,639
It means..

931
01:22:18,080 --> 01:22:24,519
Allah alone is sufficient as an aid for us...

932
01:22:25,080 --> 01:22:27,359
...and He is the best Protector.

933
01:22:30,120 --> 01:22:31,759
Beautiful.

934
01:22:35,920 --> 01:22:37,839
My Holofira.

935
01:22:50,920 --> 01:22:54,159
I will win this time, Osman.

936
01:22:54,680 --> 01:22:56,639
Sorry, Bala.

937
01:22:57,200 --> 01:22:59,999
But you will fall behind. I will win.

938
01:23:00,440 --> 01:23:02,319
You say so?

939
01:23:03,480 --> 01:23:04,759
Yes.

940
01:23:06,840 --> 01:23:09,799
Hey, don't look at me
like this. You are cheating.

941
01:23:10,080 --> 01:23:13,439
Not cheating but loving you, my Osman.

942
01:23:17,640 --> 01:23:20,039
Come on, Alaca!

943
01:23:20,520 --> 01:23:23,799
Well... Come on, Iltutan

944
01:23:46,560 --> 01:23:50,759
You cheated, Bala. But I will
show you what my love means.

945
01:23:51,440 --> 01:23:54,159
It's my love, Osman!

946
01:24:02,000 --> 01:24:03,679
Bala!

947
01:24:10,760 --> 01:24:12,359
Bala!

948
01:24:20,520 --> 01:24:22,199
My Bala..

949
01:24:22,520 --> 01:24:24,279
Bala.

950
01:24:24,920 --> 01:24:27,719
-Are you alright?
-I'm fine, Osman.

951
01:24:54,760 --> 01:24:56,279
Bala?

952
01:25:01,960 --> 01:25:03,519
Osman.

953
01:25:13,240 --> 01:25:15,079
Bala.

954
01:25:18,640 --> 01:25:20,919
Bala!

955
01:25:29,760 --> 01:25:31,519
My Bala.

956
01:25:47,280 --> 01:25:49,159
Osman.

957
01:26:06,080 --> 01:26:07,879
Bala? Bala!

958
01:26:08,800 --> 01:26:11,919
Bala. Bala.

959
01:26:14,040 --> 01:26:16,719
My Bala, you will be alright.

960
01:26:17,080 --> 01:26:19,999
-You'll be alright.
-Osman.

961
01:26:22,200 --> 01:26:23,959
My Dark Osman.

962
01:26:24,640 --> 01:26:27,519
My love...

963
01:26:28,480 --> 01:26:31,359
-I'll tell you something.
-Go ahead.

964
01:26:31,720 --> 01:26:33,359
Go ahead.

965
01:26:33,520 --> 01:26:35,719
Speak, my Bala.

966
01:26:36,320 --> 01:26:40,439
-What did we say?
-What did we say?

967
01:26:42,320 --> 01:26:46,839
The one who loves the most runs faster.

968
01:26:49,600 --> 01:26:52,959
Yes. Don't worry. We will run together again.

969
01:26:53,160 --> 01:26:55,199
We will run together again.

970
01:26:56,440 --> 01:26:58,799
Bala, hold on.

971
01:27:03,840 --> 01:27:09,039
I bear witness that there is none
worthy of worship except Allah

972
01:27:13,320 --> 01:27:21,759
...and I bear witness that
Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.

973
01:27:43,960 --> 01:27:48,439
Bala. Bala..

974
01:27:50,280 --> 01:27:51,799
Bala.

975
01:27:53,160 --> 01:27:54,999
Bala.

976
01:28:10,640 --> 01:28:12,119
My Allah.

977
01:28:12,720 --> 01:28:15,199
May You let it be a good sign.

978
01:28:35,280 --> 01:28:37,719
May Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.

979
01:28:38,760 --> 01:28:41,559
May Allah's mercy and blessings be upon you.

980
01:28:46,360 --> 01:28:48,399
My Allah.

981
01:28:50,560 --> 01:28:52,999
You're the One Who protects, my Allah.

982
01:28:54,360 --> 01:28:57,039
You're the One Who forgives.

983
01:28:57,920 --> 01:29:03,639
Even if I never stopped
worshiping You in this world

984
01:29:04,400 --> 01:29:08,839
...my gratitude could never
be enough for Your gifts.

985
01:29:09,160 --> 01:29:10,999
I know that.

986
01:29:11,480 --> 01:29:16,719
You gave me my state, my people, my family,

987
01:29:17,640 --> 01:29:20,839
...my love in this world, my wife.

988
01:29:21,440 --> 01:29:23,799
You gave me my Bala.

989
01:29:25,680 --> 01:29:27,119
My Allah.

990
01:29:28,520 --> 01:29:30,639
If Bala weren't in this world

991
01:29:32,160 --> 01:29:34,639
..colors would fade away.

992
01:29:35,440 --> 01:29:38,239
And all the sounds would go silent.

993
01:29:38,560 --> 01:29:41,199
Don't let me lose Bala.

994
01:29:41,560 --> 01:29:44,279
Don't test me with this, my Allah.

995
01:29:45,000 --> 01:29:47,079
Please let both of us..

996
01:29:47,400 --> 01:29:50,799
...walk together in this
path until our last day.

997
01:29:57,880 --> 01:30:00,639
Halime.

998
01:30:00,640 --> 01:30:02,679
My Halime.

999
01:30:03,800 --> 01:30:05,799
Halime.

1000
01:30:06,800 --> 01:30:09,159
Bala..

1001
01:30:12,629 --> 01:30:15,719
Kayi Tents

1002
01:30:28,480 --> 01:30:30,599
My Alaeddin.

1003
01:30:30,600 --> 01:30:32,959
My Gonca.

1004
01:30:40,600 --> 01:30:42,839
You've been looking bad since yesterday.

1005
01:30:42,840 --> 01:30:45,206
Did something happen? Tell me.

1006
01:30:45,218 --> 01:30:47,359
There is something but...

1007
01:30:49,160 --> 01:30:52,599
I don't know how to say it, Alaeddin.

1008
01:30:59,640 --> 01:31:01,759
Come.

1009
01:31:05,520 --> 01:31:07,119
My Gonca.

1010
01:31:07,400 --> 01:31:10,999
Are you sad because the
duty was given to Holofira?

1011
01:31:13,760 --> 01:31:16,359
Yes. Right.

1012
01:31:17,920 --> 01:31:21,519
My mother wants Hatuns
to get along with Holofira.

1013
01:31:22,120 --> 01:31:24,079
And she is doing the right thing.

1014
01:31:24,880 --> 01:31:26,759
But..

1015
01:31:27,920 --> 01:31:29,959
...she sometimes forgets about me...

1016
01:31:32,600 --> 01:31:34,519
Look..

1017
01:31:37,240 --> 01:31:39,559
How can someone forget you, Hatun?

1018
01:31:41,960 --> 01:31:43,839
They can't, right.

1019
01:31:44,080 --> 01:31:45,279
Sure not.

1020
01:31:52,240 --> 01:31:53,959
My mother is just, my rose.

1021
01:31:54,400 --> 01:31:57,399
I know.

1022
01:31:57,400 --> 01:32:00,279
My mother thinks of all of us.
-Right. Right.

1023
01:32:01,760 --> 01:32:03,319
But..

1024
01:32:03,560 --> 01:32:06,399
I know how to make you smile.

1025
01:32:07,200 --> 01:32:09,199
How?

1026
01:32:23,520 --> 01:32:25,759
Alaeddin..

1027
01:32:29,160 --> 01:32:30,999
Yes... Right, my rose.

1028
01:32:32,800 --> 01:32:35,919
May your beautiful face always smile, my Gonca.

1029
01:32:37,520 --> 01:32:41,159
Look, this will help you and your nerves.

1030
01:32:41,200 --> 01:32:42,519
Right, Trickster Hatun?

1031
01:32:42,520 --> 01:32:44,319
Yes, Scholar, yes.

1032
01:32:46,320 --> 01:32:48,399
Now I am leaving.

1033
01:32:48,840 --> 01:32:50,319
May Allah protect you.

1034
01:32:50,320 --> 01:32:52,279
May Allah protect you too, my Bey.

1035
01:32:52,280 --> 01:32:53,399
Alright.

1036
01:33:01,720 --> 01:33:03,049
Let's go.

1037
01:33:11,320 --> 01:33:13,959
How am I going to tell this to you, Alaeddin?

1038
01:33:16,840 --> 01:33:19,839
Karesiogullari Beylic

1039
01:33:33,600 --> 01:33:36,839
Why did you call us here in a rush, Karesi Bey?

1040
01:33:38,200 --> 01:33:40,279
There is important news.

1041
01:33:43,840 --> 01:33:46,639
Osman Bey is inviting me for a hunt.

1042
01:33:49,680 --> 01:33:51,399
Hunt means union.

1043
01:33:52,360 --> 01:33:53,999
Will you..

1044
01:33:54,200 --> 01:33:56,559
...make an alliance with Osman?

1045
01:33:57,920 --> 01:33:59,519
If I was going to do that...

1046
01:33:59,520 --> 01:34:01,879
...you would not be standing before me.

1047
01:34:04,800 --> 01:34:12,359
Osman is calling me for a
hunt, but you are the prey, Hatun.

1048
01:34:15,640 --> 01:34:17,799
What does that mean, Karesi Bey?

1049
01:34:19,040 --> 01:34:26,599
Osman will organize a hunt with me
today and make himself seem like a prey...

1050
01:34:27,880 --> 01:34:34,159
...and you will lose your lives
as you are trying to kill him.

1051
01:34:43,600 --> 01:34:45,279
I will not fall into this trap.

1052
01:34:47,280 --> 01:34:49,159
Karesi Bey.

1053
01:34:50,200 --> 01:34:51,719
If I hadn't told you..

1054
01:34:56,120 --> 01:34:59,839
...Osman would've done
all those things to you...

1055
01:35:05,240 --> 01:35:06,639
We will go and hunt today.

1056
01:35:08,000 --> 01:35:10,959
You will decide the rest.

1057
01:35:31,080 --> 01:35:33,519
Attention! Osman Bey.

1058
01:35:40,340 --> 01:35:44,514
I hope you return with the good
news of your vengeance, my Bey.

1059
01:35:44,514 --> 01:35:46,239
May your hunt be blessed

1060
01:35:46,240 --> 01:35:48,279
God willing my Bala, God willing.

1061
01:35:48,520 --> 01:35:51,646
It's time to send those
who threaten our people

1062
01:35:51,658 --> 01:35:54,599
and our state seven
layers beneath the earth.

1063
01:35:56,040 --> 01:35:58,159
May your market be prosperous, Bala.

1064
01:36:01,760 --> 01:36:03,239
Bring the horses.

1065
01:36:03,520 --> 01:36:05,719
The hunting time has come.

1066
01:36:05,840 --> 01:36:07,439
Come on sisters.

1067
01:36:36,080 --> 01:36:37,639
Come on, we are going to Sogut!

1068
01:36:54,600 --> 01:36:56,359
Come on Alps!

1069
01:36:56,360 --> 01:36:57,519
Come on brothers!

1070
01:36:58,320 --> 01:37:01,399
We will set the traps as
quickly as possible, come on!

1071
01:37:02,000 --> 01:37:04,079
Yes my Bey.

1072
01:37:05,480 --> 01:37:06,759
Brother..

1073
01:37:07,280 --> 01:37:10,239
Do you think we angered our Bey too much?

1074
01:37:11,400 --> 01:37:15,587
Brother, we didn't know what to say before
our Bey because we were mad at Begum Hatun.

1075
01:37:15,599 --> 01:37:16,999
Exactly.

1076
01:37:17,520 --> 01:37:20,119
We didn't. And he told
us that. And he was right.

1077
01:37:22,600 --> 01:37:25,279
But I wish we could tell him about our problems.

1078
01:37:25,440 --> 01:37:28,559
Brother, once this hunting
is over, we will speak.

1079
01:37:29,920 --> 01:37:31,599
Come on Alps!

1080
01:37:31,880 --> 01:37:34,839
The direction of the
enemy's arrival, the direction

1081
01:37:34,851 --> 01:37:37,879
of their escape, and every
path will have a trap set.

1082
01:37:38,760 --> 01:37:42,039
-Come on lions! Come on!
-Yes my Bey.

1083
01:37:51,920 --> 01:37:53,999
Are the preparations completed?

1084
01:37:54,040 --> 01:37:57,999
My Bey, as you ordered, our Alps
are setting traps all around the forest.

1085
01:37:58,040 --> 01:38:00,054
It will be completed
soon, God willing.

1086
01:38:00,066 --> 01:38:01,399
This area on the hill...

1087
01:38:01,480 --> 01:38:06,919
When I meet with Karesi, that will
be the best place for them to strike me.

1088
01:38:08,880 --> 01:38:13,679
As you said, we've placed the
most secret traps near that location.

1089
01:38:27,720 --> 01:38:29,479
Traps are good.

1090
01:38:29,480 --> 01:38:32,279
But what if she does not fall into the trap?

1091
01:38:32,360 --> 01:38:34,439
My Bey, we saw the Hatun.

1092
01:38:34,760 --> 01:38:36,959
Her mind works like a devil's.

1093
01:38:37,200 --> 01:38:39,919
We need to take other precautions.

1094
01:38:39,960 --> 01:38:42,039
My brother is right.

1095
01:38:42,800 --> 01:38:45,479
If she doesn't fall into
the trap when she comes...

1096
01:38:45,480 --> 01:38:48,079
...your life will be in danger, my Bey.

1097
01:38:49,720 --> 01:38:53,799
For this reason, the traps need to be
set on the paths as soon as possible.

1098
01:38:54,320 --> 01:38:56,039
You're right.

1099
01:38:56,040 --> 01:39:00,347
But no matter how much a hunter knows tricks,
the prey will always find a way. Boran.

1100
01:39:00,359 --> 01:39:01,799
My bey.

1101
01:39:01,800 --> 01:39:03,959
You will prepare all the traps.

1102
01:39:03,960 --> 01:39:07,159
-That woman will never pass through here.
-Yes, my Bey.

1103
01:39:07,360 --> 01:39:09,479
The spear won't fit in the sack now.

1104
01:39:10,160 --> 01:39:12,279
A storm will break out here today.

1105
01:39:12,600 --> 01:39:15,479
But they will be the ones who die. Come on.

1106
01:39:42,200 --> 01:39:44,319
Gonca.

1107
01:39:44,320 --> 01:39:47,279
You have more effort
than her in the marketplace.

1108
01:39:47,920 --> 01:39:49,879
Bala is not being fair to you.

1109
01:39:50,200 --> 01:39:51,279
Open your eyes.

1110
01:39:56,400 --> 01:39:58,359
Whatever my mother does..

1111
01:39:58,360 --> 01:40:03,359
...she does it to fix the relations between
Holofira and Kayi Hatuns, Begum Hatun.

1112
01:40:05,640 --> 01:40:10,079
If you keep justifying them like
this, you will be left here like this.

1113
01:40:11,040 --> 01:40:12,639
Doesn't it upset you, Gonca?

1114
01:40:15,680 --> 01:40:18,359
It surely upsets me.

1115
01:40:19,480 --> 01:40:21,479
They ignore me.

1116
01:40:27,040 --> 01:40:29,839
But what can I do? There's nothing I can do.

1117
01:40:39,160 --> 01:40:40,839
Sometimes..

1118
01:40:42,680 --> 01:40:44,759
...we must know our places...

1119
01:40:45,440 --> 01:40:47,799
...and accept our fates, Begum Hatun.

1120
01:40:48,840 --> 01:40:50,079
Even if you accept it...

1121
01:40:50,840 --> 01:40:55,559
..I won't allow this treatment
and injustice towards you.

1122
01:41:06,280 --> 01:41:08,879
Osman prepared his own end with his game.

1123
01:41:10,440 --> 01:41:12,759
He put his head in front of my sword.

1124
01:41:13,000 --> 01:41:18,199
Everything is ready, Sofia, but
you know Osman better than I do.

1125
01:41:20,480 --> 01:41:22,679
What if you fall into his trap?

1126
01:41:23,000 --> 01:41:24,759
Osman is in my hands.

1127
01:41:26,320 --> 01:41:30,079
They are too blind to see the
death that is approaching them.

1128
01:41:33,120 --> 01:41:35,959
You say we will be the hell of Kayis.
-Yes.

1129
01:41:42,520 --> 01:41:45,799
I've waited for years for revenge, Lukas.

1130
01:41:47,400 --> 01:41:48,719
I lived for today.

1131
01:41:52,920 --> 01:41:55,599
I won't stop you from hunting him, Sofia.

1132
01:41:56,120 --> 01:42:00,879
Today, those goat herders will
become a wounded and helpless herd.

1133
01:42:09,200 --> 01:42:11,439
Commander Lukas.

1134
01:42:11,560 --> 01:42:15,359
The disease in Akhisar may
have affected these horses as well.

1135
01:42:15,440 --> 01:42:17,639
Just in case, you...
-There is no need.

1136
01:42:19,920 --> 01:42:22,039
Pray that these horses are not sick.

1137
01:42:22,840 --> 01:42:25,759
Otherwise, you'll die
under the nails of my horse.

1138
01:43:30,280 --> 01:43:32,999
Osman Bey will learn your name.

1139
01:43:33,040 --> 01:43:37,799
But first, let me go after you
and see what you're planning.

1140
01:44:00,200 --> 01:44:02,079
Gonca Hatun.

1141
01:44:02,600 --> 01:44:05,999
Since Holofira Hatun will
sell goods in the marketplace...

1142
01:44:06,160 --> 01:44:08,599
...you should take care of the caravan.

1143
01:44:09,520 --> 01:44:12,879
You choose the goods
that will come to the caravan.

1144
01:44:13,760 --> 01:44:16,439
If my mother allows, I'll do it, Begum Hatun.

1145
01:44:16,440 --> 01:44:19,519
Begum Hatun.

1146
01:44:23,360 --> 01:44:25,039
I gave the duty to Holofira.

1147
01:44:27,680 --> 01:44:30,679
It's not a problem for me, mother Bala.

1148
01:44:36,760 --> 01:44:39,199
Come for a second.

1149
01:44:44,400 --> 01:44:45,999
What are you trying to do?

1150
01:44:46,400 --> 01:44:49,039
Are you giving orders against my orders?

1151
01:44:51,400 --> 01:44:52,799
Bala Hatun.

1152
01:44:52,880 --> 01:44:55,759
I thought I was controlling the marketplace.

1153
01:44:55,760 --> 01:45:00,799
If I can't decide who will take care
of the caravans, then why am I here?

1154
01:45:01,000 --> 01:45:03,999
Your problem is not with the caravan, Begum.

1155
01:45:04,360 --> 01:45:05,639
Of course not.

1156
01:45:07,400 --> 01:45:08,879
Gonca is very upset.

1157
01:45:09,680 --> 01:45:11,359
And I brought justice.

1158
01:45:11,520 --> 01:45:14,879
-Are you questioning my justice Begum?
-Not at all.

1159
01:45:16,040 --> 01:45:18,759
I am just doing my duty.

1160
01:45:19,920 --> 01:45:22,399
Gonca knows the marketplace better.

1161
01:45:23,160 --> 01:45:24,959
Mother..

1162
01:45:26,000 --> 01:45:29,119
If it's going to be a
problem, I won't take the task.

1163
01:45:29,800 --> 01:45:31,559
Begum Hatun..

1164
01:45:31,680 --> 01:45:35,439
-...just thought I...
Is there a need for her to think of you, Gonca?

1165
01:45:35,600 --> 01:45:38,319
There is, that's why I do, Bala Hatun.

1166
01:45:39,480 --> 01:45:45,519
As the person responsible for the market, I
can only entrust such a big trade to Gonca.

1167
01:45:48,200 --> 01:45:51,319
If you say I don't have
the authority to do so...

1168
01:45:52,000 --> 01:45:54,879
...then I am asking you to dismiss me.

1169
01:46:02,800 --> 01:46:05,119
What are we going to do Bala mother?

1170
01:46:05,240 --> 01:46:07,239
Shall we split the goods in two?

1171
01:46:07,520 --> 01:46:12,879
Holofira, you are responsible for the
goods that will be sold in the marketplace.

1172
01:46:13,400 --> 01:46:18,279
Gonca, you will take care of the
goods to be prepared for the caravan.

1173
01:46:19,280 --> 01:46:20,799
Yes mother.

1174
01:46:38,960 --> 01:46:40,479
My Bey.

1175
01:46:40,960 --> 01:46:42,719
Karesi Bey is coming.

1176
01:46:45,480 --> 01:46:47,479
Let him come

1177
01:47:20,960 --> 01:47:24,199
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you, too.

1178
01:47:25,320 --> 01:47:27,239
Peace be upon you, too.

1179
01:47:28,480 --> 01:47:30,479
Karesi Bey.

1180
01:47:34,720 --> 01:47:36,799
Come. Come.

1181
01:47:43,680 --> 01:47:45,439
Take a seat here.

1182
01:47:46,080 --> 01:47:47,879
Thank you.

1183
01:47:50,520 --> 01:47:51,839
You surprised me...

1184
01:47:52,080 --> 01:47:56,039
...with your invitation a lot, Osman Bey.

1185
01:47:56,520 --> 01:47:58,639
You wanted to join the council of beys,

1186
01:47:59,080 --> 01:48:02,439
...discuss with us and go to the hunt.

1187
01:48:03,760 --> 01:48:05,599
You are elder than us.

1188
01:48:05,840 --> 01:48:09,759
So I wanted to listen to my elder.

1189
01:48:11,360 --> 01:48:14,319
I wanted to make your wishes come true today.

1190
01:48:14,640 --> 01:48:16,759
Thank you.

1191
01:48:17,680 --> 01:48:21,639
Those who respect elders shall be
happy in this world and the afterlife

1192
01:48:21,680 --> 01:48:23,519
..our ancestors said.

1193
01:48:24,160 --> 01:48:25,839
May you be happy.

1194
01:48:25,960 --> 01:48:27,399
Thank you.

1195
01:48:30,000 --> 01:48:31,559
In these frontiers..

1196
01:48:31,800 --> 01:48:35,199
...where we had many battles
and defeated countless heathens

1197
01:48:36,080 --> 01:48:39,959
...you and I are different sides.

1198
01:48:44,400 --> 01:48:46,519
We... Both of us...

1199
01:48:47,240 --> 01:48:51,319
...fight for our cause in Allah's path.

1200
01:48:52,760 --> 01:48:58,159
We have the same destination and the same cause.

1201
01:48:58,480 --> 01:49:00,439
So tell me.

1202
01:49:01,080 --> 01:49:04,919
Why are our ways separate?
Have you every thought?

1203
01:49:05,800 --> 01:49:07,599
I have.

1204
01:49:08,800 --> 01:49:12,119
Nafs(self), Osman Bey.

1205
01:49:12,520 --> 01:49:15,399
Although the intentions are good,

1206
01:49:15,600 --> 01:49:20,759
...nafs (self) says it wants to lead the way.

1207
01:49:21,440 --> 01:49:26,319
Well... It's the fruit of
the ambition inside us...

1208
01:49:27,320 --> 01:49:32,119
...which makes our sides different.

1209
01:49:33,600 --> 01:49:35,319
Yes, nafs (self).

1210
01:49:36,200 --> 01:49:37,959
Nafs (self).

1211
01:49:38,240 --> 01:49:39,959
Well..

1212
01:49:40,480 --> 01:49:42,839
It's a trap if you get overwhelmed by it.

1213
01:49:43,720 --> 01:49:45,759
But if you can beat your nafs (self)...

1214
01:49:46,880 --> 01:49:49,079
...it's a great weapon.

1215
01:49:49,640 --> 01:49:55,959
So you say I'm one of
those who fall into the trap.

1216
01:49:56,680 --> 01:50:00,999
And you are one of those who hold the weapon.

1217
01:50:01,960 --> 01:50:05,639
-Is that so, Osman Bey?
-Karesi Bey.

1218
01:50:07,200 --> 01:50:08,799
I'm a hunter here.

1219
01:50:09,240 --> 01:50:13,439
But why do you think you're
the prey to fall into the trap?

1220
01:50:14,920 --> 01:50:18,919
I'm neither a hunter nor a prey, Osman Bey.

1221
01:50:19,400 --> 01:50:25,159
I'm a high plane tree whose
shadow both of them run under.

1222
01:50:26,960 --> 01:50:28,799
You say so?

1223
01:50:30,160 --> 01:50:31,719
Thank you.

1224
01:50:32,720 --> 01:50:36,479
Come on then. Well..

1225
01:50:36,560 --> 01:50:39,479
Let's hunt under your shadow.

1226
01:50:40,480 --> 01:50:42,239
Here we go.

1227
01:50:50,440 --> 01:50:53,639
-After you.
-Alright.

1228
01:51:07,120 --> 01:51:09,079
Come on, alps.

1229
01:51:22,240 --> 01:51:24,439
Have a safe journey.

1230
01:51:27,520 --> 01:51:30,679
You thought well about
selling these goods in Sogut.

1231
01:51:31,280 --> 01:51:33,679
Sogut got s thanks to you.

1232
01:51:34,880 --> 01:51:38,079
We all got lifeful, Ulgen.

1233
01:51:40,520 --> 01:51:44,039
Hatuns, thanks for your efforts.

1234
01:51:44,560 --> 01:51:46,559
Stalls look wonderful.

1235
01:51:46,760 --> 01:51:49,359
Thanks to you, Holofira Hatun.

1236
01:51:49,840 --> 01:51:52,319
It happened thanks to all of you.

1237
01:52:00,640 --> 01:52:04,159
Listen. If you stand strong like this,

1238
01:52:04,160 --> 01:52:07,119
...they'll get used to you
quickly. That's what they do.

1239
01:52:07,119 --> 01:52:09,159
They like pushing the new bride.

1240
01:52:10,560 --> 01:52:12,359
You say so?

1241
01:52:16,120 --> 01:52:19,519
Come on. Gonca!

1242
01:52:25,400 --> 01:52:27,079
I said Gonca.

1243
01:52:28,440 --> 01:52:31,719
-What's the matter?
-I'm so confused, Ulgen.

1244
01:52:36,320 --> 01:52:37,919
Well..

1245
01:52:39,760 --> 01:52:41,879
I need to talk to my mother.

1246
01:53:04,280 --> 01:53:06,479
We're under attack!

1247
01:53:40,480 --> 01:53:42,839
He's running off! Catch him!

1248
01:54:16,680 --> 01:54:18,599
When you draw the bow

1249
01:54:19,000 --> 01:54:24,959
...do you ever think "what if I'm
the prey at the point of the arrow"?

1250
01:54:40,960 --> 01:54:43,199
The dog who doesn't walk well...

1251
01:54:43,920 --> 01:54:45,879
..will draw wolves to the herd.

1252
01:54:46,320 --> 01:54:48,559
I fell among the dogs at times.

1253
01:54:48,760 --> 01:54:51,079
I sometimes became the prey while hunting.

1254
01:54:51,680 --> 01:54:54,919
But I'm still a wolf.

1255
01:54:55,160 --> 01:54:59,999
And I can beat a thousand
of dogs when it's time.

1256
01:55:15,560 --> 01:55:18,239
They're about to come here.

1257
01:55:29,160 --> 01:55:30,399
My Bey.

1258
01:55:32,560 --> 01:55:34,399
Our scouts have sent a message.

1259
01:55:34,720 --> 01:55:38,119
-They're coming from that way.
-Who is coming?

1260
01:55:40,040 --> 01:55:41,999
Hunters, Karesi Bey.

1261
01:55:43,040 --> 01:55:44,679
Don't worry.

1262
01:55:44,960 --> 01:55:46,599
Nobody will hurt you.

1263
01:55:46,680 --> 01:55:49,079
I'm the prey at the point of the arrow.

1264
01:55:49,400 --> 01:55:55,239
And you're a high plane tree
whose shadow we will run under.

1265
01:56:00,280 --> 01:56:01,959
Come on.

1266
01:56:23,680 --> 01:56:29,079
How can I tell my mother
about this? Oh Begum Hatun...

1267
01:56:29,560 --> 01:56:31,439
What have you done?

1268
01:56:32,480 --> 01:56:34,039
Well..

1269
01:56:35,440 --> 01:56:37,119
I can't help it.

1270
01:56:37,640 --> 01:56:39,319
I have to tell my mother.

1271
01:56:40,400 --> 01:56:43,599
They attacked the caravan!
They attacked the caravan!

1272
01:56:44,440 --> 01:56:45,759
Mother.

1273
01:56:47,600 --> 01:56:48,959
Yes, dear.

1274
01:56:49,400 --> 01:56:52,119
I need to talk to you about an urgent matter.

1275
01:56:52,440 --> 01:56:54,119
What is it?

1276
01:57:07,000 --> 01:57:08,279
Mother.

1277
01:57:11,560 --> 01:57:14,479
-I am...
Bala Hatun. Bala Hatun.

1278
01:57:15,680 --> 01:57:18,959
-The caravan. It got attacked.
-What?

1279
01:57:19,440 --> 01:57:24,359
Attacked? Prepare the horses
immediately. We're leaving!

1280
01:57:45,720 --> 01:57:48,359
Do you feel the blood smell on the air, Hristo?

1281
01:57:49,000 --> 01:57:52,919
Shortly, this place will be
stained with Turkish blood.

1282
01:57:53,640 --> 01:57:56,519
Place the soldiers behind the trees.

1283
01:57:57,240 --> 01:58:02,279
I'll start avenging Arkadius and
all our brothers with Bala Hatun.

1284
01:58:02,560 --> 01:58:04,159
Hide the horses!

1285
01:58:04,560 --> 01:58:07,439
Get behind the trees!
Bala will be here soon.

1286
01:58:10,080 --> 01:58:11,479
Bala Hatun?

1287
01:58:12,160 --> 01:58:13,799
Oh no.

1288
01:58:41,680 --> 01:58:43,879
Come on, hurry up.

1289
01:58:48,560 --> 01:58:51,879
Osman's rat is you, huh?

1290
01:58:56,600 --> 01:58:58,399
I know who you are!

1291
01:58:59,920 --> 01:59:01,479
Stableman.

1292
01:59:05,720 --> 01:59:08,079
You'll never be able to inform Osman.

1293
01:59:08,640 --> 01:59:10,959
While you see just one

1294
01:59:11,680 --> 01:59:13,239
...Osman Bey sees a thousand.

1295
01:59:13,560 --> 01:59:16,559
You'll be destroyed with your plans, Lukas.

1296
01:59:26,880 --> 01:59:28,519
Stableman.

1297
01:59:42,080 --> 01:59:43,439
Soldiers!

1298
01:59:49,760 --> 01:59:51,039
What now?

1299
01:59:51,240 --> 01:59:53,919
He can't live long with that wound.

1300
01:59:55,400 --> 01:59:57,519
We will wait for Bala.

1301
02:00:13,640 --> 02:00:15,399
My Bey, arrow!

1302
02:00:17,160 --> 02:00:19,119
You snake!

1303
02:00:36,480 --> 02:00:38,439
We're drawing back!

1304
02:01:06,560 --> 02:01:07,399
Come on, alps!

1305
02:01:07,800 --> 02:01:10,999
We'll draw them here to
the smoke. Aykurt, burn it!

1306
02:01:11,400 --> 02:01:12,999
As you order, my Bey.

1307
02:01:13,680 --> 02:01:14,999
Let's go.

1308
02:01:35,760 --> 02:01:37,599
They are over here!

1309
02:01:44,960 --> 02:01:48,359
Sons. Boran, Cerkutay.
You come with me.

1310
02:01:48,600 --> 02:01:50,599
The rest will split up.

1311
02:02:02,000 --> 02:02:04,959
Let them come.

1312
02:02:20,600 --> 02:02:22,239
Come on!

1313
02:02:46,200 --> 02:02:48,399
Boran, Cerkutay. Move!

1314
02:02:54,360 --> 02:02:56,079
Now!

1315
02:03:04,160 --> 02:03:05,959
Come on, Boran.

1316
02:03:28,480 --> 02:03:30,279
Catch him!

1317
02:03:45,720 --> 02:03:48,719
You two, go that way. You come with me!

1318
02:04:00,400 --> 02:04:02,839
Not now.

1319
02:04:04,320 --> 02:04:07,159
Not now. Come on!

1320
02:05:13,040 --> 02:05:15,559
My Allah, give me strength.

1321
02:05:15,640 --> 02:05:17,279
Give me strength.

1322
02:05:19,160 --> 02:05:20,959
I have to inform Osman Bey.

1323
02:05:30,080 --> 02:05:33,479
He must have gone this way.
Hurry up. Let's catch that traitor!

1324
02:06:08,800 --> 02:06:11,279
Hold on, Ilbay. Hold on.

1325
02:06:18,920 --> 02:06:21,319
Split up. Split up.

1326
02:06:30,480 --> 02:06:32,959
Come here.

1327
02:06:36,880 --> 02:06:38,879
You all come.

1328
02:07:21,800 --> 02:07:23,799
Wait for a second.

1329
02:07:24,560 --> 02:07:27,479
Come here, demon.

1330
02:07:30,440 --> 02:07:32,279
Come to me.

1331
02:07:39,800 --> 02:07:41,759
Come here.

1332
02:07:41,920 --> 02:07:45,359
You said you'd show your face
only when you killed me, huh?

1333
02:07:48,200 --> 02:07:54,039
Whoever attempts to mess
with my nation and state...

1334
02:07:54,720 --> 02:07:59,079
...has no rights to see the daylight or breathe.

1335
02:08:14,000 --> 02:08:16,239
Come here.

1336
02:08:31,360 --> 02:08:33,999
My Bey, that's not her.

1337
02:08:34,880 --> 02:08:37,399
This isn't the hatun who abducted us.

1338
02:08:37,600 --> 02:08:38,759
What?

1339
02:08:48,840 --> 02:08:50,399
How come?

1340
02:08:58,440 --> 02:09:00,119
Why are they so late?

1341
02:09:00,200 --> 02:09:02,519
Didn't they get the news about the attack?

1342
02:09:05,720 --> 02:09:07,319
Sofia.

1343
02:09:08,640 --> 02:09:09,879
They're coming.

1344
02:09:10,160 --> 02:09:11,759
Bala and her daughter-in-laws.

1345
02:09:12,520 --> 02:09:14,959
Osman? What about Osman?

1346
02:09:15,920 --> 02:09:18,639
He thinks he hunted me down.

1347
02:09:22,200 --> 02:09:26,199
When he takes off the
mask, he'll see he is the prey.

1348
02:09:26,760 --> 02:09:29,279
I'd love to see that moment.

1349
02:09:30,680 --> 02:09:33,799
I'm the hunter today, Lukas.

1350
02:09:34,040 --> 02:09:37,479
Today will be Osman's darkest day.

1351
02:09:40,040 --> 02:09:45,399
Bala, Holofira, Gonca... I will kill them all.

1352
02:10:06,560 --> 02:10:08,439
My Allah, give me strength.

1353
02:10:33,440 --> 02:10:35,039
I'm coming, my Bey.

1354
02:10:35,120 --> 02:10:36,559
I'm coming.

1355
02:10:38,440 --> 02:10:40,799
She has sent another one instead, huh?

1356
02:10:42,160 --> 02:10:44,559
She knew we prepared a trap for her.

1357
02:10:45,960 --> 02:10:48,079
She deceived us.

1358
02:10:51,520 --> 02:10:53,159
Well..

1359
02:10:53,600 --> 02:10:57,999
How did that snake woman
know we made a plan for her?

1360
02:11:04,760 --> 02:11:06,079
Karesi Bey!

1361
02:11:11,880 --> 02:11:14,479
I knew you'd bring the heathens here.

1362
02:11:15,000 --> 02:11:18,719
But how did you learn about my plan?

1363
02:11:25,440 --> 02:11:27,079
Obviously,

1364
02:11:28,120 --> 02:11:31,079
..there is a spy among us!

1365
02:11:45,600 --> 02:11:50,559
You invited me to the hunt and I joined.

1366
02:11:50,760 --> 02:11:52,879
I don't know about the rest.

1367
02:11:55,360 --> 02:11:57,239
Where is your respect again?

1368
02:11:57,520 --> 02:11:59,719
You blame me again!

1369
02:12:00,960 --> 02:12:03,039
Here is the respect!

1370
02:12:03,920 --> 02:12:05,759
Karesi Bey.

1371
02:12:09,160 --> 02:12:10,719
Now tell me.

1372
02:12:11,120 --> 02:12:13,119
Who told you about the plan?

1373
02:12:20,120 --> 02:12:21,999
My Bey!

1374
02:12:22,600 --> 02:12:24,399
My Bey!

1375
02:12:29,800 --> 02:12:31,279
My Bey. -Ilbay.

1376
02:12:32,560 --> 02:12:33,999
He is injured. -Alaeddin..

1377
02:12:36,360 --> 02:12:38,319
Come.

1378
02:12:43,840 --> 02:12:45,599
Karesi Bey...

1379
02:12:45,600 --> 02:12:47,199
Come.

1380
02:12:50,800 --> 02:12:54,639
My Bey. -What happened to you?
-My Bey, Lukas... Lukas, my Bey...

1381
02:12:56,680 --> 02:12:58,639
He made a treacherous plan...

1382
02:12:59,640 --> 02:13:01,399
..with a woman named Sofia.

1383
02:13:02,840 --> 02:13:04,119
Who?

1384
02:13:04,520 --> 02:13:05,639
Sofia.

1385
02:13:08,000 --> 02:13:09,399
Osman.

1386
02:13:09,720 --> 02:13:13,359
This might be the last time
you are seeing your daughter.

1387
02:13:19,000 --> 02:13:20,439
Sofia?

1388
02:13:22,440 --> 02:13:24,959
Didn't you kill that Hatun named Sofia...

1389
02:13:24,960 --> 02:13:26,439
...years ago?

1390
02:13:27,560 --> 02:13:29,719
Sofia..

1391
02:13:31,760 --> 02:13:33,599
My Bey, how is this possible?

1392
02:13:40,880 --> 02:13:43,599
My Bey... My Bey... They will..

1393
02:13:45,720 --> 02:13:48,439
...lure Bala Hatun to a trap in Karacam.

1394
02:13:49,240 --> 02:13:50,359
It's..

1395
02:13:50,720 --> 02:13:52,399
..it's that snake!

1396
02:13:52,920 --> 02:13:55,599
But Karacam is very far from here, my Bey!

1397
02:13:55,600 --> 02:13:56,919
Mother..

1398
02:13:56,920 --> 02:13:58,879
My mother's life is in danger, father!

1399
02:13:58,880 --> 02:14:00,879
My mother is in danger! -Sofia!

1400
02:14:02,040 --> 02:14:03,879
Alps, to the horses! Turan!

1401
02:14:04,840 --> 02:14:06,519
Take Ilbay to the tribe.

1402
02:14:33,160 --> 02:14:35,159
Be careful.

1403
02:14:36,200 --> 02:14:38,199
Check the Alps.

1404
02:14:44,480 --> 02:14:47,639
What happened here?

1405
02:14:57,840 --> 02:15:00,039
Welcome to your funeral, Bala.

1406
02:15:05,000 --> 02:15:06,559
You snake.

1407
02:15:06,560 --> 02:15:08,199
You played a game, huh?

1408
02:15:08,200 --> 02:15:09,999
Show me your face, you coward!

1409
02:15:10,360 --> 02:15:12,239
Don't worry.

1410
02:15:12,920 --> 02:15:14,919
You will see my face today Bala.

1411
02:15:16,480 --> 02:15:18,039
Kill them all!

1412
02:15:18,040 --> 02:15:20,599
No one will survive here!

1413
02:15:23,160 --> 02:15:25,159
Attack!

1414
02:15:46,880 --> 02:15:48,119
Begum!

1415
02:15:49,960 --> 02:15:52,159
I will kill you with my own hands!

1416
02:15:52,160 --> 02:15:53,759
I am your angel of death.

1417
02:15:54,200 --> 02:15:56,679
You will die today, Bala.

1418
02:15:56,680 --> 02:16:00,239
Before you die, I will give
you such a secret that...

1419
02:16:00,240 --> 02:16:02,919
...you will beg me to live.

1420
02:17:14,080 --> 02:17:15,799
Bala.

1421
02:17:18,080 --> 02:17:19,397
Osman.

1422
02:17:19,799 --> 02:17:21,039
Goodbye Bala.

1423
02:17:23,480 --> 02:17:25,799
Bala.

1424
02:18:00,920 --> 02:18:03,718
I see that you are really happy today Sofia.

1425
02:18:04,440 --> 02:18:07,119
I've waited so long for this day Lukas.

1426
02:18:08,638 --> 02:18:10,439
So long.

1427
02:18:19,120 --> 02:18:21,317
Be careful.

1428
02:18:23,000 --> 02:18:25,638
Check the Alps, come on!

1429
02:18:33,680 --> 02:18:35,638
What happened here?

1430
02:18:43,480 --> 02:18:45,679
Brother..

1431
02:18:51,680 --> 02:18:54,279
Come on.

1432
02:19:01,638 --> 02:19:02,959
Welcome, Bala!

1433
02:19:10,480 --> 02:19:12,317
Trap

1434
02:19:12,959 --> 02:19:14,599
Be careful, be careful.

1435
02:19:20,558 --> 02:19:22,999
We were not done.

1436
02:19:23,000 --> 02:19:24,679
Devil..

1437
02:19:25,840 --> 02:19:30,279
You attempted to hurt my daughter,
I will kill you with my own hands!

1438
02:19:30,280 --> 02:19:33,397
Aren't you going to ask what
happened to Osman, Bala?

1439
02:19:33,718 --> 02:19:36,718
He was going to hunt me, right?

1440
02:19:38,320 --> 02:19:39,599
Osman.

1441
02:19:41,080 --> 02:19:43,039
How do you know that?

1442
02:19:43,040 --> 02:19:44,679
I know everything, Bala.

1443
02:19:46,959 --> 02:19:49,359
I wish you could die with Osman but...

1444
02:19:51,720 --> 02:19:53,279
I will kill you today.

1445
02:19:53,960 --> 02:19:55,679
Those are courageous words...

1446
02:19:55,760 --> 02:19:57,919
...for a scared woman, you devil!

1447
02:20:04,800 --> 02:20:07,159
Scared woman? -Right!

1448
02:20:07,160 --> 02:20:11,359
You are scared, since you
are hiding your face! But today...

1449
02:20:11,360 --> 02:20:12,839
..you will see hell.

1450
02:20:13,120 --> 02:20:15,199
When you find out who I am..

1451
02:20:17,240 --> 02:20:20,319
...you will be really surprised, Bala.
-Show me then!

1452
02:20:21,080 --> 02:20:26,039
Attack!

1453
02:20:40,680 --> 02:20:43,159
I will take my brother's revenge!

1454
02:20:43,160 --> 02:20:46,039
Unfortunately, you won't live that long, Begum.

1455
02:21:17,480 --> 02:21:18,719
Show me your face!

1456
02:21:19,240 --> 02:21:20,759
Surprise me as you said!

1457
02:21:32,560 --> 02:21:34,519
Sofia.

1458
02:21:37,720 --> 02:21:39,879
How did you..

1459
02:21:39,880 --> 02:21:41,919
I did not die, Bala.

1460
02:21:41,920 --> 02:21:44,999
But you will die today.

1461
02:22:07,680 --> 02:22:09,719
Sofia..

1462
02:22:36,000 --> 02:22:39,599
I've waited for today for so long, Bala...

1463
02:22:42,560 --> 02:22:47,519
I took an oath to be your
Azrael. Before you die...

1464
02:22:47,520 --> 02:22:49,479
...I will...

1465
02:22:49,480 --> 02:22:51,999
...give you such a secret that...

1466
02:22:53,840 --> 02:22:57,599
You will beg me to live!

1467
02:22:59,560 --> 02:23:01,999
That will never happen Sofia!

1468
02:23:02,000 --> 02:23:03,199
Never.

1469
02:23:36,934 --> 02:23:38,244
Sofia.